.","source_citation":"Wang et al. (2022), Wind-Driven Mechanisms for the Variations of the Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent Based on Adjoint Sensitivity Analysis, Frontiers in Marine Science 9:908939, doi:10.3389/fmars.2022.908939.","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_regional_background_synthesis","source_locator":"Introduction opening paragraph, printed p1 (PDF page 1); different model/transport supports in sections 2.1–2.2 and Figures 1/2, printed pp3–4.","source_quality_note":"Original publisher p1 width and p4 transport/velocity context visually inspected. Background 400 km is not a derived width from the adjoint experiment. Underlying historical width method and exact attribution remain unreviewed.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.908939/full","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","time_convention":"Background synthesis in a 2022 article; no dated width occupation or monthly width climatology. Simulation years and transport/velocity climatologies have different support.","uncertainty_km":null,"whole_current_representative":false,"width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","width_range_km":null,"width_rank_eligible":false},{"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"approximate_width_km":200,"boundary_rule":"Approximate author-reported background width; no paired edges or boundary threshold directly resolved. Transport cutoff is not adopted as this width method.","calendar_months":null,"current_id":"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent","extraction_method":"Approximate breadth transcribed from visually inspected institutional original; no contour, transport or coordinate digitization.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"geographic_scope":"Atlantic eastward subsurface equatorial jet, called Lomonosov current; Brazil to Gulf of Guinea background description without paired boundary coordinates or a specified transverse sectio