 paired width edges or threshold resolved.","calendar_months":null,"current_id":"kuroshio-extension","extraction_method":"Approximate width transcribed from visually inspected original; no contour, coordinate or velocity-profile digitization.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"geographic_scope":"Intense Kuroshio Extension jet in monthly mean fields, extending eastward from Japan to the date line; no transverse boundary coordinates extracted.","id":"kuroshio-extension-sasaki-2013-monthly-field-width","is_confidence_interval":false,"layer":"Surface SSH and geostrophic velocity context; no fixed vertical width layer supplied.","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","name":"Kuroshio Extension","observed_period":null,"original_regional_context":{"analysis_period_context":{"end":"2010-12","is_width_measurement_support":false,"start":"1993-01"},"analysis_period_is_width_occupation":false,"audit_file":"research/kuroshio-extension-sasaki-2013-width-averaging-scope-audit.json","audit_sha256":"dfa44d57f053ac0cd8af32abcfdb0c5dcbdc63a3937c64abf14c79a2cb9370c7","axis_search_contours_are_width_edges":false,"boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"climatological_scale_context":{"geographic_scope":"Japan coast near 35°N to 165°E","is_range_endpoint":false,"is_width_sample":false,"meridional_scale_km":200,"source_locator":"Printed p445, section 3 first paragraph / Figure 1a","temporal_operator":"climatological_mean","uncertainty_km":null},"climatological_scale_is_width_range_endpoint":false,"data_context":{"grid":"1/3 degree Mercator","low_pass_context":"9-month running mean for low-frequency analyses; Figure 1a standard deviations explicitly filtered; Figure 1b monthly mean distinct.","mean_dynamic_topography":"Rio and Hernandez (2004)","product":"AVISO monthly absolute dynamic height and surface geostrophic velocities"},"display_caption":"Monthly mean fields · approximate 100 km meridional jet width, extending to the date line. No dated width series, numerical uncertainty, paired edges or annual range extracted.","display_method_note":"Separate context: the climatological jet has a reported 200 km meridional scale from Japan to 165°E. Different temporal and geographic supports; no 100–200 km seasonal range. Farther downstream, shifts of the narrow jet broaden its long-term mean. January 2005 illustrates a monthly SSH field; 60–120 cm contours locate the axis search region, not width edges.","eof_anomaly_scale_is_width_measurement":false,"illustrative_figure_date_is_width_occupation":false,"illustrative_figure_month":"2005-01","jet_displacement_is_width_variation":false,"low_pass_shading_is_monthly_width_series":false,"meridional_width_is_flow_normal_width":false,"monthly_mean_is_dated_width_series":false,"protocol_file":"plans/kuroshio-extension-width-averaging-protocol-v1.md","protocol_sha256":"bac962694f1a0f2e0560218ace30240e3f0f8716ef5e4a8edef53c0bd7f99d79","temporal_operator":"monthly_mean","underlying_width_methods_reviewed":false,"underlying_width_source":"Original section 3 and Figure 1; axis method inspected separately from unresolved paired width method.","width_passage_visually_inspected":true},"phase_kind":"regional_summary","phase_label":"Meridional jet width in monthly mean fields","range_interpretation":"One approximate regional background value; no numerical uncertainty, range, confidence interval, annual extrema or seasonal observations supplied.","range_kind":"approximate_regional_point_no_reported_interval","remaining_gates":["Resolve a reproducible meridional width boundary rule and exact transverse support.","Extract dated compatible sections before seasonal dimensions or playback.","Independent scientific admission."],"seasonal_playback_eligible":false,"section_geometry":null,"section_orientation":"Author-reported meridional width; not assumed normal to the meandering jet.","source_citation":"Sasaki, Y. N., S. Minobe and N. Schneider (2013), Decadal Response of the Kuroshio Extension Jet to Rossby Waves: Observation and Thin-Jet Theory, JPO 43(2):442–456, doi:10.1175/JPO-D-12-096.1.","source_evidence_kind":"published_original_regional_monthly_field_summary","source_locator":"Printed p445 / PDF page 5, section 3 first paragraph; data/methods pp443–444; Figure 1 printed p444 / PDF page 4.","source_quality_note":"Monthly mean is a temporal operator, not a recovered month-by-month width series. The separate 200 km climatological meridional scale has different support; it is not an interval endpoint.","source_retrieved_date":"2026-10-08","source_url":"https://eprints.lib.hokudai.ac.jp/repo/huscap/all/52934/jpo-d-12-096.1.pdf","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","time_convention":"Monthly mean fields summarized in source prose; no dated width series extracted. January 2005 is the illustrative Figure 1b field.","uncertainty_km":null,"whole_current_representative":false,"width_metric":"author_reported_current_width","width_range_km":null,"width_rank_eligible":false},{"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"approximate_width_km":null,"boundary_rule":"Author-reported order-of-magnitude less-than band size. Exceeding 80 cm/s describes speed, not an adopted width-edge cutoff.","calendar_months":null,"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent","extraction_method":"Qualifier and reference size transcribed from visually inspected original; no profile digitization, exact crossing pairing or doubled downstream value.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"geographic_scope":"Local bands near the western exit of Vitiaz Strait; downstream central Bismarck Sea widening retained as context, not a whole-current dimension.","id":"ngcu-zenk-1999-vitiaz-width-constraint","is_confidence_interval":false,"layer":"Subsurface slope-parallel current described near 200 m. No fixed width layer or paired depth-specific edges extracted.","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","name":"New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent","observed_p