.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers20-05/010028590.pdf#page=13","status":"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical","time_convention":"November 1965–May 1968 Bora/Cyclone cruise-study context. No individual dates assigned to width range endpoints; not seasonal climatology or annual extrema.","time_precision":"multicruise_context_width_endpoint_dates_unresolved","uncertainty_km":null,"whole_current_representative":false,"width_metric":"author_reported_geostrophic_current_width_range","width_metric_label":"historical local geostrophic width range","width_range_km":[300,900],"width_rank_eligible":false},{"annual_extrema_eligible":false,"approximate_width_km":120,"boundary_rule":"Author-described surface vein span. Exact seasonal velocity-anomaly threshold and paired geographic edges not specified in this descriptor. Figure 3 half-maximum anomaly-standard-deviation region is a different operator.","calendar_months":null,"current_id":"new-guinea-coastal-current","extraction_method":"Author prose values transcribed from visually reviewed original. No velocity/SST edges digitized and no averaging of regional descriptors.","fixed_layer_bounds_m":null,"full_width_inference_eligible":false,"geographic_scope":"Surface current-anomaly vein east of Vitiaz Strait, near southern New Britain; excludes the strait itself.","id":"ngcc-radenac-2016-winter-east-099","is_confidence_interval":false,"layer":"Surface altimetric current anomaly or SST-associated surface water-mass vein, depending on metric. No uniform depth slab; 50-100 m upwelling and deeper NGCUC support not transferred.","measurement_type":"published_regional_summary","name":"New Guinea Coastal Current","observed_period":null,"original_regional_context":{"audit_file":"research/ngcc-radenac-2016-seasonal-vein-width-scope-audit.json","audit_pointer":"/measurements/0","audit_sha256":"223405cce3aa4a5fecdf94dd25ebff225a9594f33fb04f784a469fd4e6e8ce10","boundary_coordinates_extracted":false,"core_offshore_distance_is_width":false,