se Gulf of Alaska gyre or an observed continuous shelf-edge jet.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean flow geography; no common fixed depth or measured current core diagnosed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Undated regional sketch using the source's naming convention. The 1977 Kodiak observations support a distinction between current names, not this full route or a simultaneous 1977 northern branch path.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/PDF/schu323/schu323.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 1.1, printed page 1 (PDF page index 4): Alaska Current northward off British Columbia/southeast Alaska; Alaskan Stream on northern/northwestern gyre arm. Section 2.1 gives Kodiak observations of the separate stream rather than a whole Alaska Current axis.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Schumacher, Reed, Grigsby and Dreves (1979), Circulation and hydrography near Kodiak Island, September to November 1977, NOAA Technical Memorandum ERL PMEL-13.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Factual geography and naming only; no source prose, charts, figures, provider geometry or observational arrays packaged.\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects offshore regional gates and every waypoint. The primary source supports northward branch identity and the stream distinction, not these coordinates, exact latitude limits or a diagnosed bathymetric contour. The route does not trace the distinct nearshore Alaska Coastal Current.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -130,\r\n      48\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -132,\r\n      51\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -135,\r\n      54\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -139,\r\n      57\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -141,\r\n      58.5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"shorter_southeast_branch\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -132,\r\n          50\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -135,\r\n          54\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n      