 the circulation convention in Favorite (1967) Figure 27. Gates truncate the schematic and are selected by OSW; they are not current origin or termination. Westward Alaskan Stream, West Wind Drift/North Pacific Current, Bering branches and downstream Alaska/California branches are excluded.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean schematic geography; source Figure 27 is a circulation schematic with transports referred to 1000 m, not a fixed-depth velocity axis. No depth-specific geometry extracted.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Undated OSW reference sketch of the author circulation schematic. Paper observations May-August 1959 provide context; this line is neither simultaneous observed geometry nor a 1959 seasonal frame.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.webapps.nwfsc.noaa.gov/assets/4/8131_09242014_161208_Favorite.1967-INPFC-Bull-21.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Printed p. 2 Background (Aleutian/Subarctic naming); pp. 11-12 Relative Currents (eastward Subarctic versus westward Alaskan Stream); p. 19 Figure 27 schematic. Cited text pages read; Figure 27 visually inspected.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Favorite, F. (1967), The Alaskan Stream, Bulletin 21, International North Pacific Fisheries Commission, pp. 1-20. Manuscript dated June 1965; publication 1967.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"US government author, NOAA-hosted publication. Only paraphrased facts and independently selected OSW geometry packaged; original figure/PDF not redistributed.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-08\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW rounded waypoints follow the eastward Subarctic branch in Figure 27. Coordinates are editorial approximations, not calibrated digitization or measured cores. The 175 E gate omits western formation/return-flow confluence; 140 W is a regional truncation before coastal branching. Alternative end at 145 W tests gate convention. Latitude shifts test drawing convention, not current width.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      175,\r\n      47.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -180,\r\n      48\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -170,\r\n      48.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -160,\r\n      49\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -150,\r\n      50\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -140,\r\n      52.5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_editorial_corridor\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          175,\r\n          46.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -180,\r\n          47\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -170,\r\n          47.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -160,\r\n          48\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -150,\r\n          49\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -140,\r\n          51.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW southern schematic convention; not a current boundary or seasonal state.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_editorial_corridor\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          175,\r\n          48.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -180,\r\n          49\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -170,\r\n          49.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -160,\r\n          50\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -150,\r\n          51\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -140,\r\n          53.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW northern schematic convention; not a current boundary or seasonal state.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"shorter_eastern_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          175,\r\n          47.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -180,\r\n          48\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -170,\r\n          48.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -160,\r\n          49\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -150,\r\n          50\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -145,\r\n          51\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW earlier truncation at 145 W, not a source-defined termination.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Four declared schematic/gate choices crossed with three uniform longitude shifts and independent endpoint latitude shifts (-0.5/0/+0.5 degrees): 108 editorial cases. Envelope is not uncertainty, physical width, seasonal extrema or a confidence interval.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review schematic identity against modern layer-compatible velocity fields and North Pacific Current naming.\",\r\n    \"Replace editorial waypoints with connected, sourced velocity-core geometry; diagnose upstream and downstream gates.\",\r\n    \"Resolve Bering and Alaska/California branches without adding overlapping components.\",\r\n    \"Acquire month/depth-resolved axes and paired boundaries before annual length or width ranges; no seasonal playback from this schematic.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1490,\r\n    130,\r\n    245,\r\n    190\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 6.5,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 9,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 1,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"175 E OSW reach gate\",\r\n    \"140 W OSW reach gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Favorite (1967), Fig. 27\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Subarctic schematic regional reach\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [],\r\n  \"context_landmarks\": [],\r\n  \"longitude_seam_policy\": \"shortest_geodesic_periodic_display\",\r\n  \"source_review_receipt\": {\r\n    \"retrieved_bytes\": 12277867,\r\n    \"retrieved_sha256\": \"a3202ace4b2f43bc3af8bf1746619b90afcc8378ee3c1bd467f459fae6995eb0\",\r\n    \"pdf_pages\": 20