al current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"tile_id\": \"level0_A_1\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a005500/a005505/perpetual_ocean2_EQUIREC_071_final_beauty_level0_A_1.mp4\",\r\n      \"source_id\": \"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"tile_id\": \"level0_B_1\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a005500/a005505/perpetual_ocean2_EQUIREC_071_final_beauty_level0_B_1.mp4\",\r\n      \"source_id\": \"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_C_4\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"1256ace4b349ed71d251f4f30f4a7296a7b137641d855c795538b05d41337974"},"research/atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared 42 W to 32 W western summer study reach: one editor-selected NECC connection inside the source regional surface-flow context. Branch assignment and joining remain review gates. Excludes independent northern-branch geometry, upstream NBC retroflection, equatorial ESC and eastern-basin continuation. Not a whole-current length or sum of branches. All latitude gates and bends are editorial.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Altimetry-derived surface geostrophic context; no fixed-depth velocity core, parcel trajectory or depth-uniform axis inferred.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route guided by the 1993-2017 boreal-summer climatological context (July-August-September). Not a dated axis, monthly mean measured centerline or year-round route.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/251/2023/os-19-251-2023.html\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2.1, 3 and 4.2 identify HS5 at 42 W and HS6 at 32 W; section 6 / Fig. 8 caption defines summer JAS. The explicit east-of-38-W branch joining description concerns fall, not a verified summer connection. All route latitudes and bends are editorial.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Dimoune et al. (2023), Revisiting the tropical Atlantic western boundary circulation from a 25-year time series of satellite altimetry data, Ocean Science 19, 251-268, doi:10.5194/os-19-251-2023.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Open-access sou