current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_B_3\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"44fbddc113fefbff554b2b652a0a62c2f965be3e8be28aa0267c381645b251be"},"research/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central Atlantic subsurface reference reach between observations at 35 W near 5 N and the central observational neighborhood at 23 W near 5 N. Connecting vertices are editorial, not an observed continuous axis. Excludes NBC/NEC source recirculation, surface NECC flow, uncertain filaments east of 28 W and farther-east termination. Not full-current source-to-end length.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Subsurface eastward NEUC context. The central mooring study defines 65–270 m; historical western cores lie near sigma-theta 26.75 kg/m3. These different vertical definitions are not imposed as one uniform layer along the reference line.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Western sections in February 1993 and April 1996; central moorings June 2006–February 2008 and November 2009–January 2018 with 2002–2018 ship sections. Editorial section-to-section geography, not simultaneous observations or an annual/seasonal axis.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Bourles et al. (1999), section 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W NEUC centered at 5 N in February 1993 and April 1996; core near sigma-theta 26.75. Sections 4.6 and 6.1 separate source retroflection from the named current; eastern filament context cites earlier work.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Bourles, Gouriou and Chuchla (1999), On the circulation in the upper layer of the western equatorial Atlantic, JGR Oceans 104(C9), 21151–21170, doi:10.1029/1999JC900058.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Source PDF states copyright 1999 American Geophysical Union; repository access does not establish an open reuse license. Facts paraphrased with attribution; no source figure or observed field copied.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects rounded 5 N vertices between separate 35 W and 23 W observational neighborhoods. Northern/southern smooth bends and alternate central gates are sensitivity choices, not source-diagnosed axes. No continuous physical connection, uniform depth, filament path, transport-loop length or seasonal position is established by this sketch.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -35,\r\n      5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -32,\r\n      5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -28,\r\n      5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -25,\r\n      5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -23,\r\n      5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_central_approach\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -35,\r\n          5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -32,\r\n          5.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -28,\r\n          5.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -25,\r\n          5.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -22.5,\r\n          5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW northern bend and later observational-neighborhood truncation, not a seasonal axis or lateral edge.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_central_approach\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -35,\r\n          5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -32,\r\n          4.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -28,\r\n          4.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -25,\r\n          4.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -23.5,\r\n          5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW southern bend and earlier central truncation, not a source filament or current width.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared reach shapes crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees: 81 editorial cases, not physical width, seasonal variation or statistical confidence.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Diagnose a compatible subsurface axis before asserting continuity across the separate section neighborhoods.\",\r\n    \"Resolve source recirculation, eastern filaments and termination before whole-current length.\",\r\n    \"Review historical two-degree latitude width with boundary and month-date precision support; no whole width or seasonal range inferred.\",\r\n    \"Keep mooring transport variability distinct from seasonal length/width geometry.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    635,\r\n    387,\r\n    115,\r\n    115\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.65,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 2.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.45,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"35 W observation context\",\r\n    \"23 W central context\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Bourles et al. (1999); Burmeister et al. (2020)\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"35 W–23 W subsurface reference reach\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://pureadmin.uhi.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/14119479/2020GL088350.pdf\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt, Claus and Hahn (2020), Fluctuations of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Associated Changes in Oxygen Transports, GRL 47, e2020GL088350, doi:10.1029/2020GL088350.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Introduction and sections 2–4, pp. 1–4: central 5 N, 23 W observations and 65–270 m definition; data intervals and fixed-box/inferred-transport distinctions.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Central observational context; weak seasonal cycle and episodic intraseasonal events do not establish seasonal geometry.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014760\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt and Duteil (2019), Interannual Variability of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Its Impact on Oxygen, JGR Oceans 124, 2348–2373, doi:10.1029/2018JC014760.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Introduction, sections 2.1 and 2.3: 23 W ship sections; model half-width and observational integration boundaries.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Distinguishes chosen transport integration widths and model-domain longitude span from diagnosed current dimensions.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"ea572bc2321949f696ad9414caaa228cbb8dc647c6fcd79a4fdfaf393cbd2398\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  