ence-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"tile_id\": \"level0_B_1\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a005500/a005505/perpetual_ocean2_EQUIREC_071_final_beauty_level0_B_1.mp4\",\r\n      \"source_id\": \"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_B_5\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/brazil-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/brazil-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"0b8bd13661715e0f7e66ed62172e9b6f768325cf57d1081b650798f2c7b27592"},"research/canary-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Source regional geography paraphrased with attribution; no source figures, curves or velocity data packaged.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.5,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 2.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.5,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review northern feed-region and Cape Blanc naming gates before length admission.\",\r\n    \"Validate offshore corridor and island clearance using finer coastline, bathymetry and suitable velocity fields.\",\r\n    \"Resolve source-specific seasonal path and Lanzarote Passage conventions before animated geometry or width extraction.\",\r\n    \"Canonical admission and publication review; no current footprint or annual extremes inferred.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"canary\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Canary Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"OSW offshore reference corridor from a regional northern source gate near 35 N, past the western Canary archipelago, to a Cape Blanc offshore departure gate near 21 N. Excludes upstream Azores/Portugal routes, the broader Iberian-to-tropical Canary Current System, Lanzarote Passage recirculation, poleward undercurrents and downstream North Equatorial Current. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean southward return-flow naming context; source descriptions mention central waters over approximately upper 200-300 m. No depth-specific velocity core or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Regional circulation geography from 2018/2026 papers, with seasonal-path caveats from 2015 observations published in 2023. Selected offshore corridor is not a dated trajectory, annual mean axis or a particular seasonal route.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/971/2018/\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 1 Introduction, first paragraph: distinguishes approximately 35-20 N named-current region from wider Canary Current System; bifurcation away from Africa near Cape Blanc (21 N) toward the North Equatorial Current.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Kounta et al. (2018), A model perspective on the dynamics of the shadow zone of the eastern tropical North Atlantic - Part 1: the poleward slope currents along West Africa, Ocean Science 14, 971-997, doi:10.5194/os-14-971-2018.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/22/2059/2026/\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Ibrahim and Sun (2026), A multidecadal sea level rise and its hiatus in the tropical Atlantic margin off northwest Africa, Ocean Science 22, 2059-2081, doi:10.5194/os-22-2059-2026.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 4 opening paragraphs: source-region convergence around 35 N and upper-layer context.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Northern geographic naming-gate context; no model axis digitized.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC019487\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Perez-Hernandez et al. (2023), The Seasonal Cycle of the Eastern Boundary Currents of the North Atlantic Subtropical Gyre, JGR Oceans 128, e2022JC019487.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Abstract and sections 1-2: regional seasonal migration and distinct Lanzarote Passage flow; Table 1 and prose disagree about fall cruise month.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Seasonal continuity caveat; no 2015 observed axis, section width, transport or annual extrema reconstructed.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Every offshore vertex and endpoint is OSW-selected. The regional source names latitude ranges and departure geography, not these longitude gates or a current axis. A western archipelago detour avoids island-centre locations but is not identified as a measured fall path. Shorter northern/southern approach gates test naming convention. No source arrows, inverse-model fields or tracks digitized.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -13.5,\r\n      35\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -14.8,\r\n      33\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -15.4,\r\n      31.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -17.5,\r\n      30\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -18.5,\r\n      28.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -18.8,\r\n      27.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -18.9,\r\n      25.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -19,\r\n      23\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -20,\r\n      21\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"shorter_feed_region_departure_gates\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -14,\r\n          34.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -14.8,\r\n          33\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -15.4,\r\n          31.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -17.5,\r\n          30\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -18.5,\r\n          28.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -18.8,\r\n          27.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -18.9,\r\n          25.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -19,\r\n          23\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -19.7,\r\n          21.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Selected shorter regional naming approaches, not measured seasonal contraction.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Two selected feed-region/Cape Blanc gate conventions crossed with longitude and independent endpoint latitude offsets -0.05/0/+0.05 degrees: 54 editorial scenarios, not seasonal variation or confidence bounds.\",\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    700,\r\n    280,\r\n    105,\r\n    125\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"35 N feed-region gate\",\r\n    \"Cape Blanc offshore gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Kounta et al. (2018), sec. 1\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Canary offshore return-flow corridor\",\r\n  \"context_landmarks\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"label\": \"Madeira\",\r\n      \"coordinate