rial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_B_2\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"93d9cf1b2390fa421475e6f87f66621d0a95661ed96a3e5421af958d4b5e3183"},"research/east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Sciascia et al. publisher states Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. Supporting Frontiers reuse terms not independently reviewed; attributed textual geography only, no source figures or velocities copied.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.25,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 2.3,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.4,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Resolve Dalmatian-name overlap before canonical naming/extent admission.\",\r\n    \"Review island passages and bathymetry with finer geography and compatible surface-current data; coarse land clearance is insufficient.\",\r\n    \"Retrieve original 2002-2003 measurements and basin drifter study before claiming diagnosed whole-current or seasonal geometry.\",\r\n    \"Do not transfer 800 km basin length, basin width, qualitative current broadening or seasonal strength into current dimensions.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"east-adriatic\",\r\n  \"name\": \"East Adriatic Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"OSW offshore eastern-Adriatic reference corridor under the Otranto-to-Istria surface-circulation convention. Gates are editorial neighborhoods, not observed origins or termination. Excludes western return flow, sub-basin recirculation loops and unverified island-channel branches. The possible Dalmatian-name overlap is unresolved and its extent is not transferred. The published 800 km basin length is not used as current length; this estimate comes from the declared OSW vertices.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"General surface-circulation geography; no velocity-defined current core or uniform intermediate/full-depth layer diagnosed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial corridor supported by published general circulation descriptions. Not the 2002-2003 local mooring trajectory, annual mean observed axis or seasonal path.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sciascia et al. (2018), Section 2.1 and Figure 1 caption: northwestward eastern Balkan coast circulation, separate western return and three sub-basin gyres. Endpoint convention from Urbini et al. (2020), Study Area, circulation paragraph.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Sciascia et al. (2018), Linking sardine recruitment in coastal areas to ocean currents using surface drifters and HF radar: a case study in the Gulf of Manfredonia, Adriatic Sea, Ocean Science 14, 1461-1482, doi:10.5194/os-14-1461-2018.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.00679/full\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Urbini et al. (2020), Temporal and Spatial Variability of the CO2 System in a Riverine Influenced Area of the Mediterranean Sea, the Northern Adriatic, doi:10.3389/fmars.2020.00679.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Study Area, general circulation paragraph: eastern-side northward flow from Otranto toward Istrian Peninsula, citing Poulain (2001).\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Regional endpoint convention; not a measured continuous current axis or named termination.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects coarse offshore vertices progressing northwest from eastern Otranto through Albanian/Dalmatian coastal neighborhoods to an offshore Istrian approach. Longitude alternatives change offshore detour placement; they are not current edges or observed width. No source arrows or drifter tracks digitized. Coarse coast clearance does not resolve the many islands or channels.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      19.1,\r\n      40\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      19,\r\n      40.75\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      18.4,\r\n      41.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      17.7,\r\n      42.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      16.6,\r\n      42.9\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      15.65,\r\n      43.45\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      14.6,\r\n      44.1\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      13.8,\r\n      44.6\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      13.25,\r\n      45\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"farther_offshore_corridor\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          19.0,\r\n          40\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          18.85,\r\n          40.75\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          18.25,\r\n          41.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          17.55,\r\n          42.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          16.450000000000003,\r\n          42.9\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          15.5,\r\n          43.45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          14.45,\r\n          44.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.65,\r\n          44.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.15,\r\n          45\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW farther-offshore corridor; excludes island-channel detail and is not a seasonal displacement.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"closer_coastal_corridor\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          19.150000000000002,\r\n          40\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          19.1,\r\n          40.75\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          18.5,\r\n          41.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          17.8,\r\n          42.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          16.700000000000003,\r\n          42.9\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          15.75,\r\n          43.45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          14.7,\r\n          44.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.9,\r\n          44.6\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          13.3,\r\n          45\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW closer coastal corridor under the same neighborhood gates; not an observed current core or shoreward edge.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared offshore corridors crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.05/0/+0.05 degrees and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.05/0/+0.05 degrees: 81 editorial scenarios; not seasonal variability, current width or confidence bounds.\",\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    828,\r\n    245,\r\n    85,\r\n    85\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"Eastern Otranto gate\",\r\n    \"Offshore Istrian gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Sciascia et al. (2018), sec. 2.1; Urbini et al. (2020)\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Otranto-Istria surface-circulation convention\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"6c6d37e3511dcbbd21ddb0f0432ad48e3487de6e5fe16c4b947756e500e711f9\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_c