ation or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_F_5\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/east-australian-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/east-australian-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"f9e903221cf97d197e7b6f2f62094fd6bd7d99fe82d852af857b1f54e31a20d8"},"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"east-greenland-coastal\",\r\n  \"name\": \"East Greenland Coastal Current\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared southeast Greenland coastal study-area reach from an OSW offshore gate near 66 N to a Cape Farewell offshore gate near 60 N. Excludes the weak northern 68 N identification, EGC shelfbreak path, Irminger Current, offshore diversions and West Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified low-salinity inner-shelf jet context from July-August 2004 hydrography and ADCP-referenced geostrophic velocity. No uniform fixed-depth axis diagnosed along this editorial path.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial regional geography informed by the July-August 2004 JR105 campaign. Not a simultaneous measured axis, annual mean or recurring summer footprint.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), section 3: Cape Farewell and 66 N section geography; section 3.5: weak assumed northern jet near 68 N; sections 8-9: merging near 63 N and approximately 1000 km shelf survey description. Relevant text inspected, no current-axis figure digitized.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), The East Greenland Coastal Current: Structure, variability, and forcing, Progress in Oceanography, accepted manuscript.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"WHOI-hosted accepted manuscript; no explicit reuse license inspected. Attributed geographic facts paraphrased; source figures and velocity fields are not copied.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects coarse offshore vertices following the southeast Greenland coastal sequence. Gates near 66 N and Cape Farewell are editorial truncations, not observed current origin/termination. Surface fresh-water wedges alone do not diagnose the jet. The 63 N merger is retained as a scope warning, not an invented separate uninterrupted branch. Coarse land avoidance does not establish inner-shelf placement. Initial southern scenarios touched the coarse land mask; the Cape Farewell approach gate was moved east to 42.9 W before regeneration. This clearance is not bathymetric validation.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -34.5,\r\n      66\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -38,\r\n      65.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -40,\r\n      64.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -40.3,\r\n      63.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -41.3,\r\n      62.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -42,\r\n      62\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -42.5,\r\n      61\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -42.9,\r\n      60\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"closer_coastal_sequence\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -34.65,\r\n          66\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -38.15,\r\n          65.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -40.15,\r\n          64.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -40.449999999999996,\r\n          63.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -41.449999999999996,\r\n          62.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -42.15,\r\n          62\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -42.65,\r\n          61\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -43.05,\r\n          60\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW coarse lateral alternative; not an observed axis, current edge or width.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"farther_offshore_sequence\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -34.35,\r\n          66\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -37.85,\r\n          65.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -39.85,\r\n          64.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -40.15,\r\n          63.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -41.15,\r\n          62.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -41.85,\r\n          62\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -42.35,\r\n          61\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -42.75,\r\n          60\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW coarse lateral alternative; not an observed axis, current edge or width.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.1,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.1\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.1,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.1\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three editorial offshore reach shapes crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.1/0/+0.1 degrees and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.1/0/+0.1 degrees: 81 scenarios. Neither an annual range nor a confidence interval.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  