ario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"606edd4cfe959e577c65a0a089b607006ed878823af280f113bba682da6af680"},"research/east-greenland-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"east-greenland\",\r\n  \"name\": \"East Greenland Current\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Regional outer/slope EGC reference corridor from the Fram Strait section at 78.5 degrees N to the study’s southern shelf boundary at 59 degrees N in the Cape Farewell region. Excludes a distinct East Greenland Coastal Current axis, interior export branches, upstream Arctic extensions and onward West Greenland Current. The 59 degrees N gate is the paper’s regional boundary, not a precise geographic coordinate of Cape Farewell.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Outer/slope EGC geographic corridor only; no velocity layer, bathymetric axis or transport diagnosed. Separate from the near-surface coastal current.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"General editorial reference corridor. The source analyzes VIKING20X and GLORYS12 during 1993–2019; this sketch is not their time-mean or instantaneous model axis.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2023JC019890\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Introduction: distinctions among EGCC, shelfbreak branch and outer/slope EGC, and Fram Strait–Cape Farewell focus. Section 2.1.1: East Greenland shelf from the 78.5 degrees N section to the 59 degrees N study boundary; Figure 1 caption identifies a 1000 m offshore shelf boundary.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Schiller-Weiss, I., Martin, T., Karstensen, J., and Biastoch, A. (2023), Do Salinity Variations Along the East Greenland Shelf Show Imprints of Increasing Meltwater Runoff?, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans 128, e2023JC019890.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"CC BY-NC article; factual geographic reference only. No source figure, contour, velocity field or provider geometry copied into this candidate.\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects coarse offshore regional waypoints and longitudes to sketch the southward east Greenland corridor. Source latitude boundaries and regional/branch description constrain the sketch; these vertices are not published model coordinates, a digitized figure path or observed current-axis positions. Source study shelf/1000 m definitions do not establish these vertices as a diagnosed isobath. An initial broad offshore sketch was revised toward the east Greenland margin; a trial 43 degrees W vertex at 61 degrees N intersected the coarse atlas land mask and was rejected.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -8,\r\n      78.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -12,\r\n      76\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -15,\r\n      73\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -21,\r\n      70\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -31,\r\n      67\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -39,\r\n      64\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -42,\r\n      61\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -43.5,\r\n      59\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three uniform longitude shifts (-0.25/0/+0.25 degrees) crossed with independent start/end latitude shifts (-0.5/0/+0.5 degrees): 27 editorial scenarios. Not a source-reported error interval and does not exhaust branch choices or meanders.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Check the coarse offshore vertices against source-defined outer/slope branch geography and a reproducible bathymetric corridor.\",\r\n    \"Independent review of the 78.5–59 degrees N regional convention and branch transitions, including convergence with the Irminger Current south of 64 degrees N.\",\r\n    \"Canonical claim, geometry and measurement integration; retain regional scope and keep coastal current separate.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    580,\r\n    80,\r\n    220,\r\n    155\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"78.5°N Fram Strait section\",\r\n    \"59°N study boundary\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Schiller-Weiss et al. (2023), §§1, 2.1.1\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"regional outer-EGC reference route\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-02\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"d0c23129e9be69c708a3fcaf5f6f39a0d18c86c254258905988771cb460cf69c\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 2670.611,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 2700,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2568.1,\r\n    2776.156\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2500,\r\n    2800\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.25,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.5,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.5,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -8.25,\r\n          78.0\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\