ot physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_E_4\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"b032ee03a0b2174c4e16fa1328e516d244d408413f464a24c90dc327cb4c0132"},"research/indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared 50-90 E eastward winter surface reach. The 50 E start is an OSW offshore truncation beyond the western confluence, and 90 E follows approximate recirculation context. Neither is a diagnosed whole-current terminus. Excludes Somali/East African source legs, the southern return into SEC, South Java continuation, equatorial Wyrtki jets and subsurface SEUC.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Source boreal winter December-March convention; Gauss-Markov seasonal climatology using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2.1-2.2: drifter support, 1993-2018 selection, fitted seasonal fields and December-March winter. Section 3 seasonal discussion after Figures 5-6: eastward SECC reaches about 90 E before recirculating into SEC; Figure 13 caption.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Wu, Du, Qian, Cheng, Wang, Zhang and Peng (2020), Structure and Seasonal Variation of the Indian Ocean Tropical Gyre Based on Surface Drifters, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans, doi:10.1029/2019JC015483.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Attributed factual context; source figures, trajectories and velocity arrays not reproduced. No open figure-reuse license inferred.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects a 50 E offshore start and a 90 E study-context truncation. A near-4 S connecting line is editorial, informed by western confluence context, not a traced core. Northern/southern middle bends and endpoint latitude offsets test drawing choices, not current edges or seasonal changes.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      50,\r\n      -4\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      60,\r\n      -4\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      70,\r\n      -4\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      80,\r\n      -4\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      90,\r\n      -4\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_drawing\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          50,\r\n          -4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          60,\r\n          -3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          70,\r\n          -3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          80,\r\n          -3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          90,\r\n          -4\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW middle-latitude drawing sensitivity, not a velocity boundary or a different season.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_drawing\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          50,\r\n          -4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          60,\r\n          -4.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          70,\r\n          -4.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          80,\r\n          -4.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          90,\r\n          -4\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW middle-latitude drawing sensitivity, not a velocity boundary or a different season.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    0\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three connecting shapes with fixed longitude gates and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.5/0/+0.5 degrees: 27 editorial cases. Not physical width, source measurement error, annual extrema or confidence.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Extract the fitted winter velocity field and diagnose current-axis and gate locations.\",\r\n    \"Resolve source-flow confluence and eastern recirculation/continuation before whole-current length.\",\r\n    \"Retain drifter sampling bias and uncertainty; drawing offsets do not estimate those errors.\",\r\n    \"Recover comparable transverse velocity edges and repeat seasonal axes before width or annual extrema.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    970,\r\n    365,\r\n    260,\r\n    180\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 4.8,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 7.2,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.8,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"50 E offshore gate\",\r\n    \"90 E recirculation context\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Wu et al. (2020), sec. 2-3\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"December-March surface studied reach\",\r\n  \"context_landmarks\": [],\r\n  \"source_season_convention\": {\r\n  