 entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/north-brazil-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/north-brazil-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"250d6b1f2c4a497dcf6461ef545536b176f01b677eb5f85acdc008cb60706257"},"research/north-cape-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"north-cape\",\r\n  \"name\": \"North Cape Current — Northern branch\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared western Hopen Deep Northern-branch study-area reach, from an OSW southern Hopen approach gate near 30 E, 75 N to the LS05 frontal/core neighborhood near 28.5 E, 77 N. Excludes Barents Sea entrance, Central branch, eastern continuations and cyclonic recirculation loops. Not the full North Cape Current or an observed trajectory.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Northern-branch Atlantic-water jet context. Fig. 9 LS05 vectors average 20–80 m; no uniform fixed-depth axis is established along this editorial reach. The separate 15-crossing fitted-width composite retains unresolved depth support.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial geographic reach informed by Morozov et al. (2017) study in 2007, with general branch geography from IMR/PINRO (2009). Not a dated observed axis, annual mean or seasonal route.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://physical-oceanography.ru/repository/issues/2017/02/05/20170205.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Stationary currents p. 38: Northern branch enters Hopen Deep and partially recirculates; Currents pp. 46–47, Fig. 1 and Fig. 9: western Hopen margin study area and LS05 current/front core near the 200 m isobath. Figures inspected for regional orientation, not digitized.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Morozov, Pavlov, Pavlova and Fedorov (2017), Polar Frontal Zone of the Barents Sea Western Trough Based on the Direct Measurements in 2007, Physical Oceanography 2, 36–50, doi:10.22449/1573-160X-2017-2-36-50.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Copyright 2017 authors and Physical Oceanography. Attributed regional facts paraphrased; no source figures, curves, velocity data or coastlines packaged.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects the southern study-area approach, intermediate western-margin waypoints and rounded LS05 frontal neighborhood. These are declared editorial gates, not source-provided paired current endpoints. Source figures establish study orientation, not a digitized current line. The section ship track is transverse and is not used as the longitudinal route. Alternative bends and endpoint offsets test coarse choices only.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      30,\r\n      75\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      29.4,\r\n      75.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      29,\r\n      76\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      28.7,\r\n      76.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      28.5,\r\n      77\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"western_margin_approach\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          29.5,\r\n          75\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          28.8,\r\n          75.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          28.2,\r\n          76\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          28.1,\r\n          76.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          28.5,\r\n          77\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative OSW study-area approach/bend; not observed seasonal migration.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"eastern_margin_approach\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          30.5,\r\n          75\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          30,\r\n          75.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          29.8,\r\n          76\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          29.2,\r\n          76.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          28.5,\r\n          77\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative OSW study-area approach/bend; no physical meander or recirculation loop reconstructed.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.1,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.1\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three editorial study-area shapes crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees and independent endpoint latitude shifts -0.1/0/+0.1 degrees: 81 sensitivity cases. Not fit uncertainty, current width or annual variability.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Validate editorial approach and LS05 core-neighborhood gates with source authors and finer bathymetry.\",\r\n    \"Resolve full Northern/Central branching paths and recirculation before whole-system dimensions.\",\r\n    \"Acquire dated velocity geometry before physical axis or meander length.\",\r\n    \"Keep 8 km Gaussian profile scale separate; no buffering, annual dimensions or footprint inference.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    875,\r\n    108,\r\n    110,\r\n    90\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.7,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 3,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.6,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"Southern Hopen approach\",\r\n    \"LS05 frontal neighborhood\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Morozov et al. (2017), pp. 38, 46–47\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"western Hopen Northern-branch reach\",\r\n  \"context_landmarks\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"label\": \"Hopen\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        25.02,\r\n        76.51\r\n      ]\r\n 