inal HTML/PDF bytes and figures not acquired or reviewed.\",\n    \"retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-21\",\n    \"original_file\": null,\n    \"original_sha256\": null,\n    \"redistribution_license\": null\n  },\n  \"measurements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"norwegian-atlantic-slope-orvik-2003-reported-length-candidate\",\n      \"dimension\": \"length\",\n      \"value_km\": 3500,\n      \"approximate\": true,\n      \"locator\": \"Introduction, paragraph [2], eastern-branch description.\",\n      \"short_excerpt\": \"eastern branch about 3500 km long\",\n      \"support\": \"Eastern shelf-edge branch along the Norwegian shelf; exact start/end gates not specified in the inspected statement.\",\n      \"statistic\": \"author_reported_approximate_branch_extent\",\n      \"observation_period\": null,\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\n      \"paired_boundary_coordinates\": null,\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\n      \"seasonal_range_km\": null,\n      \"calculation\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"norwegian-atlantic-slope-orvik-2003-reported-mean-width-candidate\",\n      \"dimension\": \"width\",\n      \"value_km\": 40,\n      \"approximate\": true,\n      \"locator\": \"Introduction, paragraph [4], Svinøy annual-mean description citing Orvik et al. (2001).\",\n      \"short_excerpt\": \"annual mean NwASC appears as a stable flow about 40 km wide\",\n      \"support\": \"Local Svinøy section; not a width along the entire branch.\",\n      \"statistic\": \"width_of_described_annual_mean_flow_not_mean_of_instantaneous_widths\",\n      \"observation_period\": null,\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\n      \"paired_boundary_coordinates\": null,\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\n      \"seasonal_range_km\": null,\n      \"calculation\": null,\n      \"cited_original_doi\": \"10.1016/S0967-0637(00)00038-8\",\n      \"independent_width_observation\": false,\n      \"existing_related_record_id\": \"norwegian-atlantic-slope-orvik-2001-regional-width\",\n      \"context_exclusions\": [\n        \"The 200–900 m isobaths describe slope bathymetry, not a fixed measurement layer.\",\n        \"The 1995–2003 transport record does not establish the exact width averaging interval.\",\n        \"The explicitly reported 40 km is not computed as a midpoint of the older 30–50 km range.\",\n        \"Annual mean does not establish annual minimum, maximum, confidence interval or seasonal samples.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"eligibility\": {\n    \"canonical_current_admitted\": false,\n    \"canonical_measurement_inventory_admitted\": false,\n    \"length_rank_eligible\": false,\n    \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\n    \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\n    \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\n    \"map_geometry_eligible\": false,\n    \"state_intersection_eligible\": false\n  },\n  \"excluded_canonical_owners\": [\"norwegian\", \"norwegian-coastal\"],\n  \"remaining_work\": [\n    \"Acquire the original article and inspect its branch map and measurement context.\",\n    \"Review proposed slope-current identity separately from ambiguous Norwegian Current and coastal flow.\",\n    \"Resolve length gates, layer and time convention before constructing route geometry.\",\n    \"Inspect the cited 2001 original before counting independent width support.\",\n    \"Acquire dated repeated boundaries for seasonal widths and lengths; do not manufacture a range from these prose estimates.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_file\": \"figures/norwegian-atlantic-slope-reported-dimensions.svg\"\n}\n","source_sha256":"c71a4198efc937b292a366d7e3aa6e5c64ac5e3109fcadb7eaf149439f0112ba"},"research/norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Source regional geography paraphrased with attribution; no source figures, curves or velocity data packaged.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.8,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 3.2,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.6,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review southern naming gate and Ingoy downstream truncation before length admission.\",\r\n    \"Validate shelf/coastal-water correspondence, island clearance and alternative local branches with finer coast and bathymetry.\",\r\n    \"Resolve Norwegian Current versus Norwegian Atlantic/Coastal naming conventions; no aliases merged.\",\r\n    \"Acquire compatible seasonal sections before numeric annual width ranges or route playback.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"norwegian-coastal\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Norwegian Coastal Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"OSW southern Norwegian Skagerrak approach to the Ingoy section at the Barents Sea entrance, following a simplified offshore coastal corridor. Excludes Baltic source-water transit, Jutland inflow, fjord circuits, offshore Norwegian Atlantic Current branches, West Spitsbergen and downstream Murman continuation. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Buoyant coastal-water naming context; no depth-specific core, full transverse section or uniform salinity footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography described by Christensen et al. (2026), with Ingoy context from Skagseth et al. (2011). Not a dated observed track, annual mean axis or seasonal geometry series.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/2785/2026/\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 1 Introduction: Norwegian Coastal Current originates in Skagerrak and flows along Norway into Barents Sea; explicitly distinguished from warm saline Norwegian Atlantic Current.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Christensen et al. (2026), Norkyst version 3: the coastal ocean forecasting system for Norway, Geoscientific Model Development 19, 2785-2798, doi:10.5194/gmd-19-2785-2026.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011JC006996\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Skagseth, Drinkwater and Terrile (2011), Wind- and buoyancy-induced transport of the Norwegian Coastal Current in the Barents Sea, JGR Oceans 116, doi:10.1029/2011JC006996.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Introduction paragraphs 3-7 and Figure 2: source-water convention, coastal route and complex Tromsoflaket pathways converging near Ingoy; data section distinguishes local measurements.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Ingoy gate context and continuity caveat; no drifter trajectory or velocity field digitized.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"All offshore vertices and approach gates are OSW-selected from named regional geography. Southern gate samples Norwegian Skagerrak approach, not Baltic origin. Alternative Skagerrak/Ingoy approaches test endpoint convention; intermediate coastal detours simplify banks and island passages and require bathymetric review. No source model grid or figure arrows digitized; qualitative seasonal descriptions do not supply annual length or width extremes.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      10.0,\r\n      58.55\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      8,\r\n      57.95\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      6.4,\r\n      57.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      4.8,\r\n      58.25\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      4.65,\r\n      59.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      4.2,\r\n      60.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      4.4,\r\n      61.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      5.0,\r\n      62.1\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      5.6,\r\n      63\r\n    ],\r\