\"scope\": \"Selected southwestward Oyashio corridor south of Bussol Strait, followed by the first intrusion along eastern Honshu, to an OSW nominal gate at 40 N. Alternative southern gates use seasonal index limits at 38.5 N in April and 41.5 N in December. Excludes upstream East Kamchatka Current, Sea of Okhotsk circuits, offshore return branch into Subarctic Current, eastward Oyashio Extension/front and detached eddies. This branch convention is not the complete Oyashio system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional corridor with a southern gate informed by the 5 C isotherm at 100 m. A temperature-defined intrusion index is not a velocity axis; no fixed-depth core or isotherm geometry extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming with alternative seasonal intrusion-index gates; 40 N is an OSW intermediate comparison choice, not an annual-mean endpoint. No contemporary dated axis or seasonal length observations.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Oyashio first-intrusion route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#oyashio-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/Qiu_EoOS2019.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"tsushima\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Tsushima Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Japanese coastal-branch reference corridor from an OSW eastern Tsushima Strait approach to a western Tsugaru Strait approach. Excludes the offshore/Korean branch, Soya continuation and the separately named Tsugaru outflow. Connecting vertices do not assert uninterrupted flow or a full-system length. Downstream merges are shared circulation context, not exclusive nearshore water-parcel continuity.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean Japanese coastal branch naming context; source distinguishes coastal and offshore pathways. No depth-specific velocity axis or thermal-front width reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General regional circulation context in Yoon et al. (2016), Yokomatsu and Kida (online 2024; issue 2025) and JMA explanatory pages. Not a contemporaneous trajectory, annual mean axis or seasonal length series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Japanese coastal branch corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2016JC011891\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"NPSW\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northwest Pacific subtropical\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"kuroshio-extension-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"kuroshio-extension\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Kuroshio Extension\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary Kuroshio Extension extent from approximately 145 to 160 degrees E, upstream of its separately named North Pacific Current. This naming convention is not a universal termination rule for all Kuroshio Extension literature; excludes the coastal Kuroshio, recirculation gyres and downstream North Pacific extent.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional flow geography; no diagnosed depth-specific jet axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial route under NOAA glossary naming limits; not a synoptic jet or time-averaged observed axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA Kuroshio Extension extent\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#kuroshio-extension-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 18,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-pacific-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-pacific\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Pacific Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary regional extent from about 160 degrees E to an OSW gate at 145 degrees W, somewhat beyond the source's approximate 150 degrees W region. Alternative ends at 150 degrees W. This convention excludes downstream Alaska/California branches and the Kuroshio Extension. It is not the entire Japan-to-North-America circulation or a universal naming extent; AMS describes a different western origin near 170 degrees W.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional reference geography; no depth-specific velocity axis extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated glossary-convention sketch; no simultaneous or climatological current axis inferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA North Pacific regional extent\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-pacific-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 108,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 162,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-middle-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - middle jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central middle NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 13 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"middle NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-middle-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - northern jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central northern NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 18 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"northern NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - southern jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central southern NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 8 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"southern NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"NPSE\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northeast Pacific subtropical\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"CCAL\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Coastal California Current\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"davidson\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Davidson Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"California-Oregon winter coastal reference corridor between OSW gates at 35 N and 46 N. These are bookkeeping gates, not source-published current endpoints. Excludes conditional Vancouver Island penetration and the deeper California Undercurrent. No full-system length or width footprint.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Seasonal northward surface-current regional context; not the separately described California Undercurrent below 200 m or a reconstructed velocity axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"October-March California-Oregon regional seasonal description in the February 1978 report; strongest flow described in January. Historical summary, not a dated trajectory, current-year observation or modern monthly climatology.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"historical winter regional corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"CHIN\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"China Sea\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"mindanao-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"mindanao-current\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Mindanao Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Southward Philippine eastern-boundary regional route from a near-surface NEC bifurcation gate at 14.3 N to an OSW southern Mindanao approach gate at 5.5 N. Excludes downstream Indonesian Throughflow, NECC and EUC routes, Mindanao and Halmahera eddy circuits, and Mindanao Undercurrent. The southern gate is an editorial regional limit, not an established whole-current endpoint.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface gate convention only; excludes the northward undercurrent and deeper bifurcation latitudes. No fixed-depth core traced.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Northern gates use near-surface annual mean and May/September climatological model conventions from 1982-1998. Alternatives change the gate, not the full seasonal velocity axis; not a measured annual length distribution.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Mindanao near-surface branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#mindanao-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003jc002013\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - northern jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central northern NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 18 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"northern NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"tsushima\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Tsushima Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Japanese coastal-branch reference corridor from an OSW eastern Tsushima Strait approach to a western Tsugaru Strait approach. Excludes the offshore/Korean branch, Soya continuation and the separately named Tsugaru outflow. Connecting vertices do not assert uninterrupted flow or a full-system length. Downstream merges are shared circulation context, not exclusive nearshore water-parcel continuity.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean Japanese coastal branch naming context; source distinguishes coastal and offshore pathways. No depth-specific velocity axis or thermal-front width reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General regional circulation context in Yoon et al. (2016), Yokomatsu and Kida (online 2024; issue 2025) and JMA explanatory pages. Not a contemporaneous trajectory, annual mean axis or seasonal length series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Japanese coastal branch corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2016JC011891\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"NPTG\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"North Pacific tropical gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"PNEC\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"North Pacific equatorial countercurrent\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared east-central Pacific study reach from 140 W to 95 W. Gates truncate a larger current; western Pacific inflow and coastal redistribution east of 95 W are excluded. Intermediate bends are editorial connections among section descriptions, not a reconstructed continuous axis or parcel trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface and upper-ocean eastward countercurrent; maxima can be slightly subsurface. Separate from equatorial EUC and deeper NSCC/Tsuchiya Jet; no uniform depth imposed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of mean section descriptions from Johnson et al. (2002). Source ensemble June 1985 through December 2000; exact regional acquisition dates and a dated route axis are not extracted. Near 110 W the source reports no eastward surface expression in December-February and an August surface maximum; this line does not imply continuous year-round flow.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"140 W to 95 W study reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared northern Tsuchiya Jet studied reach from the 155 W mean-section core to the 110 W mean-section core. Western formation and basin continuation east of 110 W are excluded. The section gates truncate a larger current; interpolating bends are editor-selected, not a measured continuous centerline or particle path.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface northern Tsuchiya Jet, distinct from upper-ocean NECC and equatorial EUC. Source Table 1 gives local mean peak depths of 220 m at 155 W and 130 m at 110 W; these are local supports, not a uniform depth or full vertical boundaries.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of mean hydrographic-section peak locations in Johnson and Moore (1997). Historical source compilation 1967-1996 has uneven sampling; no exact regional observation period, monthly axis or dated route reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W northern Tsuchiya reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared historical southern mean-core studied reach from 155 W 3.5 S to 110 W 5.5 S. These gates truncate the larger southern subsurface flow. Western formation, secondary-jet geometry and eastern continuation are excluded. This is one study-defined connection, not an aggregate centerline or sum of primary and secondary branches.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Southern subsurface/Tsuchiya flow. Johnson and Moore (1997) Table 1 gives local mean peak depths 250 m at 155 W and 160 m at 110 W; no uniform depth or full vertical bounds imposed. Later observations resolve primary and deeper secondary jets; their correspondence to this historical mean-core route remains a review gate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of Johnson and Moore (1997) mean section support from a historical 1967-1996 CTD compilation. No exact regional observation dates, annual mean measured axis or monthly geometry reconstructed. Rowe et al. (2000) branch observations are separate context, not a second route or annual evolution series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W historical southern mean-core reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"CAMR\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Central American coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"caribbean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"caribbean\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Caribbean Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Selected westward Caribbean regional route from a Windward Islands approach to the Belize/Yucatan transition near 19 N. Excludes the northward Yucatan Current, Loop and Florida currents, additional island entry branches, Colombia-Panama gyre circuits and eddy perimeters. No unique continuous axis or whole-system length asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface regional geography; no fixed-depth velocity axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional convention informed by 1996-2001 near-surface drifter circulation; not a dated trajectory or extracted mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Caribbean regional corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#caribbean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002GL016231\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared east-central Pacific study reach from 140 W to 95 W. Gates truncate a larger current; western Pacific inflow and coastal redistribution east of 95 W are excluded. Intermediate bends are editorial connections among section descriptions, not a reconstructed continuous axis or parcel trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface and upper-ocean eastward countercurrent; maxima can be slightly subsurface. Separate from equatorial EUC and deeper NSCC/Tsuchiya Jet; no uniform depth imposed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of mean section descriptions from Johnson et al. (2002). Source ensemble June 1985 through December 2000; exact regional acquisition dates and a dated route axis are not extracted. Near 110 W the source reports no eastward surface expression in December-February and an August surface maximum; this line does not imply continuous year-round flow.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"140 W to 95 W study reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"SUND\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Sunda–Arafura shelves\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"mindanao-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"mindanao-current\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Mindanao Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Southward Philippine eastern-boundary regional route from a near-surface NEC bifurcation gate at 14.3 N to an OSW southern Mindanao approach gate at 5.5 N. Excludes downstream Indonesian Throughflow, NECC and EUC routes, Mindanao and Halmahera eddy circuits, and Mindanao Undercurrent. The southern gate is an editorial regional limit, not an established whole-current endpoint.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface gate convention only; excludes the northward undercurrent and deeper bifurcation latitudes. No fixed-depth core traced.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Northern gates use near-surface annual mean and May/September climatological model conventions from 1982-1998. Alternatives change the gate, not the full seasonal velocity axis; not a measured annual length distribution.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Mindanao near-surface branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#mindanao-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003jc002013\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - southern jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central southern NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 8 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"southern NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 9,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"WARM\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Western Pacific warm pool\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"New Ireland Coastal Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared regional east-coast New Ireland reach from an OSW southeastern offshore gate near 153.6 E, 4.5 S to an OSW northern offshore gate near 150.9 E, 2.2 S. Excludes Solomon Strait inflow across the basin, New Britain and St Georges branches, Bismarck Sea westward continuation, retroflection and downstream EUC route. Gates are editorial truncations, not whole-current origin or termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface thermocline boundary-current geography. Grenier et al. discuss density-dependent modeled pathways; no single fixed-depth axis or whole-depth current footprint extracted for this coastal reach.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial geographic reach informed by source background and ORCA025-G70 modeled pathways. The simulation covers 1958–2004, while analysis excludes the 2002 forcing adjustment and ends in 2001. These dates are study context, not exact observations, a measured annual mean axis or seasonal route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"east New Ireland regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#new-ireland-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011JC007477\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-middle-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - middle jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central middle NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 13 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"middle NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-middle-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - northern jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central northern NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 18 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"northern NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific NEUC - southern jet\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central southern NEUC component reach between OSW 135 E and 175 E gates. Near-western latitude context is 8 N; all connecting latitudes and bends are editorial. Excludes other NEUC components, 3 N SCC/Tsuchiya jet, western source paths and eastern continuation. Not a whole-component or parent-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Argo P-vector absolute geostrophic zonal velocity on 27.0 sigma-theta (kg/m3), spatially varying depth. Not LICOM/SODA velocity, uniform depth, or the 3 N Tsuchiya jet.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"2004-2014 Argo climatological mean, year precision; not a dated observed axis or monthly geometry. Model periods 1969-2007 are not transferred.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"southern NEUC isopycnal reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-neuc-southern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-35469-2\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Editorial eastern Solomon Islands reach between offshore gates near 162.0 E, 9.6 S and 155.8 E, 4.6 S, following island-chain geography toward northeast Bougainville. Excludes the SEC upstream basin, Solomon Strait crossing, New Ireland coastal continuation and EUC. Source descriptions establish regional context; continuity between gates is unresolved. These are OSW truncations, not observed origins or termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface thermocline context of the 2010 model proposal. Its indexed mean-flow discussion uses sigma 24.0-26.5, not a fixed 100-400 m slab. The later 2012 ADCP averages and tracer profiles do not supply one common continuous SICU core layer.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Static OSW geographic reference. The 2010 model mean and July-August 2012 regional observations are separate evidence contexts. Neither dates these editorial vertices or establishes seasonal route changes.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"eastern Solomon Islands reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"PEQD\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Pacific equatorial divergence\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared east-central Pacific study reach from 140 W to 95 W. Gates truncate a larger current; western Pacific inflow and coastal redistribution east of 95 W are excluded. Intermediate bends are editorial connections among section descriptions, not a reconstructed continuous axis or parcel trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface and upper-ocean eastward countercurrent; maxima can be slightly subsurface. Separate from equatorial EUC and deeper NSCC/Tsuchiya Jet; no uniform depth imposed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of mean section descriptions from Johnson et al. (2002). Source ensemble June 1985 through December 2000; exact regional acquisition dates and a dated route axis are not extracted. Near 110 W the source reports no eastward surface expression in December-February and an August surface maximum; this line does not imply continuous year-round flow.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"140 W to 95 W study reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-necc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared northern Tsuchiya Jet studied reach from the 155 W mean-section core to the 110 W mean-section core. Western formation and basin continuation east of 110 W are excluded. The section gates truncate a larger current; interpolating bends are editor-selected, not a measured continuous centerline or particle path.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface northern Tsuchiya Jet, distinct from upper-ocean NECC and equatorial EUC. Source Table 1 gives local mean peak depths of 220 m at 155 W and 130 m at 110 W; these are local supports, not a uniform depth or full vertical boundaries.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of mean hydrographic-section peak locations in Johnson and Moore (1997). Historical source compilation 1967-1996 has uneven sampling; no exact regional observation period, monthly axis or dated route reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W northern Tsuchiya reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared historical southern mean-core studied reach from 155 W 3.5 S to 110 W 5.5 S. These gates truncate the larger southern subsurface flow. Western formation, secondary-jet geometry and eastern continuation are excluded. This is one study-defined connection, not an aggregate centerline or sum of primary and secondary branches.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Southern subsurface/Tsuchiya flow. Johnson and Moore (1997) Table 1 gives local mean peak depths 250 m at 155 W and 160 m at 110 W; no uniform depth or full vertical bounds imposed. Later observations resolve primary and deeper secondary jets; their correspondence to this historical mean-core route remains a review gate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of Johnson and Moore (1997) mean section support from a historical 1967-1996 CTD compilation. No exact regional observation dates, annual mean measured axis or monthly geometry reconstructed. Rowe et al. (2000) branch observations are separate context, not a second route or annual evolution series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W historical southern mean-core reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"HUMB\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Humboldt Current coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-pacific\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Pacific Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 103 W to 88 W eastern regional studied reach between two reported Subtropical Front crossings associated with the SPC in the source regional surface circulation. Front locations are proxies, not diagnosed velocity-core endpoints, and were observed in different years. OSW connecting vertices and alternatives are editorial. Branch correspondence is unresolved. Excludes Chatham Rise/western basin, ACC export branch, Peru-Chile coastal flow, northward recirculation and independent split bands. Not a whole-current or simultaneous observed axis.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface drifter circulation context combined with separate hydrographic STF crossing locations. The 14 C at 150 m frontal criterion does not define a 150 m current axis; drifter velocities include ageostrophic flow. No fixed-depth velocity centerline reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"1979–2004 regional drifter mean is context; P18 frontal crossing was sampled February–April 1994 and P19 February–April 1993. This editorial connection does not combine them into one dated trajectory or infer seasonal geometry.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"STF-proxy regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2024-12/010047303.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"AUSE\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"East Australian coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"east-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-australian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"East Australian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Coherent poleward shelf-break jet from about 15 degrees S to the usual separation around 32 degrees S; excludes Tasman Front and downstream eddy/extension routes.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Jet geographic description; no velocity layer or depth integration diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General geographic reference sketch; not the instantaneous model surface-speed snapshot in Figure 1 or a dated observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"coherent-jet reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/3853/2026/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"hiri-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"hiri-current\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Hiri Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Broad Hiri naming convention: northward Australian boundary branch from an OSW 15 S bifurcation approach, clockwise around the Gulf of Papua entrance, to an OSW eastern Louisiade approach. Excludes closed gyre return circuits, direct mid-basin Solomon inflow, EAC, downstream New Guinea currents and eddy excursions. Narrower literature uses Hiri only south of PNG and proposes Gulf of Papua Current for the connected boundary system; no alias merge or complete system extent admitted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional geography; no fixed-depth current core or vertically integrated streamline reconstructed. Source northern bifurcation descriptions have different depth support.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming convention drawing on 2018 modeled context and 1993 circulation descriptions; not one simultaneous dated field, an annual mean route or seasonal length measurement.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"broad Hiri regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#hiri-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2017JC013221\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Solomon Island Coastal Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Editorial eastern Solomon Islands reach between offshore gates near 162.0 E, 9.6 S and 155.8 E, 4.6 S, following island-chain geography toward northeast Bougainville. Excludes the SEC upstream basin, Solomon Strait crossing, New Ireland coastal continuation and EUC. Source descriptions establish regional context; continuity between gates is unresolved. These are OSW truncations, not observed origins or termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface thermocline context of the 2010 model proposal. Its indexed mean-flow discussion uses sigma 24.0-26.5, not a fixed 100-400 m slab. The later 2012 ADCP averages and tracer profiles do not supply one common continuous SICU core layer.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Static OSW geographic reference. The 2010 model mean and July-August 2012 regional observations are separate evidence contexts. Neither dates these editorial vertices or establishes seasonal route changes.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"eastern Solomon Islands reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#solomon-island-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://faculty.washington.edu/kessler/abstracts/melet_etal_2010.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-australian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Australian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Winter South Australian component from the eastern Great Australian Bight region to the western approaches of Bass Strait under Ridgway and Condie's naming convention. Nominal offshore regional gates at 135.5 and 142.5 degrees E are OSW choices. Excludes Leeuwin flow west of the Bight, Zeehan continuation off Tasmania, gulf outflows and summer reversal. Does not allocate every transition region of the 5,500 km system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean shelf-edge geography; no depth-averaged velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Austral-winter naming convention; editorial geography rather than an observed winter trajectory or year-round eastward current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter South Australian component\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 4,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 4\r\n    },\r\n    \"ARCH\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Archipelagic deep basins\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"east-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-australian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"East Australian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Coherent poleward shelf-break jet from about 15 degrees S to the usual separation around 32 degrees S; excludes Tasman Front and downstream eddy/extension routes.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Jet geographic description; no velocity layer or depth integration diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General geographic reference sketch; not the instantaneous model surface-speed snapshot in Figure 1 or a dated observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"coherent-jet reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/3853/2026/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"hiri-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"hiri-current\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Hiri Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Broad Hiri naming convention: northward Australian boundary branch from an OSW 15 S bifurcation approach, clockwise around the Gulf of Papua entrance, to an OSW eastern Louisiade approach. Excludes closed gyre return circuits, direct mid-basin Solomon inflow, EAC, downstream New Guinea currents and eddy excursions. Narrower literature uses Hiri only south of PNG and proposes Gulf of Papua Current for the connected boundary system; no alias merge or complete system extent admitted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional geography; no fixed-depth current core or vertically integrated streamline reconstructed. Source northern bifurcation descriptions have different depth support.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming convention drawing on 2018 modeled context and 1993 circulation descriptions; not one simultaneous dated field, an annual mean route or seasonal length measurement.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"broad Hiri regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#hiri-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2017JC013221\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"leeuwin-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"leeuwin\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Leeuwin Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Source-convention Leeuwin component from the North West Cape regional gate near 22 degrees S, southward around Cape Leeuwin and eastward into the central Great Australian Bight. Nominal eastern gate 130 degrees E uses the source's winter water-mass penetration convention; alternative 125 degrees E tests a shorter central-Bight naming convention. Excludes the North West Shelf, offshore eddies, South Australian and Zeehan components. Not the full 5,500 km boundary-flow system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Shelf-edge upper-ocean reference geography; no fixed-depth or diagnosed velocity axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial reference route under the source's autumn/winter southern-extension convention; not a simultaneous or climatological measured axis, nor a guaranteed summer path.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Leeuwin component into the Bight\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#leeuwin-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 21,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-surface-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n          \"name\": \"New Guinea Coastal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 146 E to 142 E offshore north-New-Guinea surface reference reach, ordered northwestward for the trade-wind convention. Both gates and every vertex are selected by OSW. Excludes southeast coastal continuation, Vitiaz Strait, Halmahera branches and the deeper New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent; not a whole-current endpoint or observed axis.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface circulation schematic only; no fixed-depth slab, velocity core or undercurrent axis extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Figure 8.6 depicts April-November trade-wind circulation; December-March northwest monsoon reverses the surface flow. This editorial sketch is not dated geometry or a monthly climatological axis. The year-round northwest flow below 200 m is excluded.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"north New Guinea surface reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#new-guinea-coastal-surface-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://ocg.aori.u-tokyo.ac.jp/member/eoka/documents/Tomczak_Godfrey.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"New Guinea Coastal Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared north-Papua New Guinea regional reach from an OSW offshore Vitiaz-downstream approach gate near 147 E, 4.5 S to the 142 E, 2.5 S mooring neighborhood. Excludes passage through Vitiaz Strait itself, upstream Solomon Sea coastal branches, New Britain and St Georges branches, and the cross-equatorial EUC connection. Gates do not establish whole-current origin or termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface thermocline flow. Ueki et al. report a local northwestward core generally at 150–250 m near the moorings; the core shoals during El Nino. This local depth support is not a fixed-depth axis assigned along the entire editorial reach. Surface New Guinea Coastal Current remains a separate identity.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial regional geographic reach informed by Ueki et al. mooring observations during 1995–2000 and Grenier et al. background/model pathways. The source reports seasonal and ENSO variations locally; this static route is not a dated observation, annual axis or observed seasonal length/width footprint. Source seasons use boreal labels: winter January–March, summer July–September, fall October–December. Unlisted months are not inferred flow absence.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"northern PNG subsurface regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#new-guinea-coastal-undercurrent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002JC001611\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-australian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Australian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Winter South Australian component from the eastern Great Australian Bight region to the western approaches of Bass Strait under Ridgway and Condie's naming convention. Nominal offshore regional gates at 135.5 and 142.5 degrees E are OSW choices. Excludes Leeuwin flow west of the Bight, Zeehan continuation off Tasmania, gulf outflows and summer reversal. Does not allocate every transition region of the 5,500 km system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean shelf-edge geography; no depth-averaged velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Austral-winter naming convention; editorial geography rather than an observed winter trajectory or year-round eastward current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter South Australian component\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 6,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    \"SPSG\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"South Pacific gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"NEWZ\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"New Zealand coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"tasman-historical-connection-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"tasman-front\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Tasman Front\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Historical Tasman Front naming convention represented by an OSW offshore 154 E to 172 E near-34 S regional connection. Gates truncate the Australia-northern-New-Zealand geography; neither coastal endpoints nor a continuously identifiable jet is claimed. Excludes coastal EAC, southern extension and East Auckland coastal continuation.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Historical upper-ocean thermal/front circulation context, not a fixed-depth velocity core. No temperature contour or measured meander digitized.\",\r\n          \"t