 \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"zeehan-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"zeehan\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Zeehan Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Winter Zeehan component from the western Bass Strait approach, southward off western Tasmania, around its southern tip and toward the southern east coast. Regional gate coordinates are OSW choices. Excludes the South Australian segment, East Australian Current and offshore eddy excursions; not the full western/southern Australian boundary-flow system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean shelf-edge reference geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source's winter boundary-flow component convention; not a simultaneous observed trajectory or guaranteed year-round path.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter Zeehan component\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#zeehan-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"OCAL\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Oceanic California Current\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"alaska-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"alaska\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Alaska Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional northward Alaska Current branch offshore British Columbia and southeast Alaska, using OSW latitude gates at 48 and 58.5 degrees N. Excludes the northern/northwestern Alaskan Stream, the distinct nearshore Alaska Coastal Current, individual fjords and offshore eddy excursions. Gate alternatives vary the regional reach; not the entire counterclockwise Gulf of Alaska gyre or an observed continuous shelf-edge jet.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean flow geography; no common fixed depth or measured current core diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated regional sketch using the source's naming convention. The 1977 Kodiak observations support a distinction between current names, not this full route or a simultaneous 1977 northern branch path.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"northward Alaska regional branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#alaska-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/PDF/schu323/schu323.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"davidson\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Davidson Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"California-Oregon winter coastal reference corridor between OSW gates at 35 N and 46 N. These are bookkeeping gates, not source-published current endpoints. Excludes conditional Vancouver Island penetration and the deeper California Undercurrent. No full-system length or width footprint.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Seasonal northward surface-current regional context; not the separately described California Undercurrent below 200 m or a reconstructed velocity axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"October-March California-Oregon regional seasonal description in the February 1978 report; strongest flow described in January. Historical summary, not a dated trajectory, current-year observation or modern monthly climatology.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"historical winter regional corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"REDS\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Red Sea and Persian Gulf\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"red-sea-saline-overflow\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Red Sea saline overflow - northern plume reference reach\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared northern descending-plume regional connection from an OSW Bab-el-Mandeb approach gate toward the Figure 1 lower-channel neighborhood. Every vertex is an independent rounded editorial choice. Excludes the other branch, gully products, late equilibrated-water spreading and a whole-parent length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Descending dense Red Sea outflow plume branch, with bottom and interfacial layers and changing equilibrium depth. Not a surface flow, fixed 100-250 m depth slab, channel width or equilibrated-water boundary undercurrent.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"REDSOX winter/summer 2001 geographic branch context; selected path is editorial, not a synoptic velocity axis or reconstructed seasonal routes. Cruises and station composites are separate occupations.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"northern descending-plume reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"redsox-southern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"red-sea-saline-overflow\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Red Sea saline overflow - southern plume reference reach\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared southern descending-plume regional connection from an OSW Bab-el-Mandeb approach gate toward the Figure 1 lower-channel neighborhood. Every vertex is an independent rounded editorial choice. Excludes the other branch, gully products, late equilibrated-water spreading and a whole-parent length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Descending dense Red Sea outflow plume branch, with bottom and interfacial layers and changing equilibrium depth. Not a surface flow, fixed 100-250 m depth slab, channel width or equilibrated-water boundary undercurrent.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"REDSOX winter/summer 2001 geographic branch context; selected path is editorial, not a synoptic velocity axis or reconstructed seasonal routes. Cruises and station composites are separate occupations.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"southern descending-plume reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#redsox-southern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Somali Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"June-July southern Somali coastal limb from an OSW equatorial gate northward to an OSW separation gate at 3.5 N. Source describes offshore departure south of 4 N and limited exchange with the northern Great Whirl. Excludes the upstream East African Coast Current, offshore Southern Gyre return limb, Great Whirl, Socotra outflow and undercurrents. This is one seasonal component, not the full summer Somali Current system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-layer southern seasonal coastal geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"June-July monsoon-onset two-gyre convention. Does not assume rare late-summer gyre coalescence or persistent whole-coast continuity.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"June-July southern coastal limb\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Somali Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northeast-monsoon southward Somali coastal branch from an OSW northern gate at 7 N to an OSW confluence gate at 3 S. Source latitude ranges are 6-8 N for divergence and 2-4 S for confluence with East African Coast Current. Excludes the northward flow north of the divergence, offshore feeder, eastward continuation, undercurrents and gyre circuits. No year-round whole-current extent asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface/upper-layer seasonal coastal reference geography; the source describes a shallow winter equatorial current, but no fixed-depth velocity axis is reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Northeast winter monsoon convention; not a simultaneous dated observation or an annual-average route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter southward coastal branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"IND W\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Western India coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Equatorial Undercurrent - spring reference reach\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared53 E to91 E spring Indian EUC reference corridor. Longitude gates follow the reviewed 1963 observational domain; OSW chooses the equatorial line, connecting vertices and alternatives. Excludes Wyrtki surface jets, westward undercurrent conventions, anomalous fall episodes and whole-basin endpoints.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-thermocline eastward undercurrent geography. No uniform fixed depth reconstructed; 80.5 E, 50-150 m observations in 1994 are a different local occupation, not this route layer.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Spring eastward convention. Review reports several observations between 53 E and 91 E during March-April 1963; those stations do not establish a simultaneous continuous axis or annual recurrence.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"spring observational-domain reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf#page=29\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 50-90 E eastward winter surface reach. The 50 E start is an OSW offshore truncation beyond the western confluence, and 90 E follows approximate recirculation context. Neither is a diagnosed whole-current terminus. Excludes Somali/East African source legs, the southern return into SEC, South Java continuation, equatorial Wyrtki jets and subsurface SEUC.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source boreal winter December-March convention; Gauss-Markov seasonal climatology using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"December-March surface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"March-May subsurface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 18,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"ARAB\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northwest Arabian Sea upwelling\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"persian-gulf-cascading-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"persian-gulf-saline-overflow\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Persian Gulf saline overflow\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northern outflow/cascading reference reach: OSW upstream truncation near 26 N, then the source-described vicinity of 25deg20N,57E and 24deg50N,56deg50E. No Arabian Sea downstream route or whole-system origin/termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Descending Persian Gulf Water core; near 220 m neutral-buoyancy description is downstream context, not a fixed 220 m trajectory or surface-current route.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"October-November1999 GOGP99 study geography. Editorial line joins regional descriptions; not one synoptic snapshot, monthly geometry or an R13 width occupation.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Northern outflow/cascading reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#persian-gulf-cascading-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00000/390/83.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Somali Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northeast-monsoon southward Somali coastal branch from an OSW northern gate at 7 N to an OSW confluence gate at 3 S. Source latitude ranges are 6-8 N for divergence and 2-4 S for confluence with East African Coast Current. Excludes the northward flow north of the divergence, offshore feeder, eastward continuation, undercurrents and gyre circuits. No year-round whole-current extent asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface/upper-layer seasonal coastal reference geography; the source describes a shallow winter equatorial current, but no fixed-depth velocity axis is reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Northeast winter monsoon convention; not a simultaneous dated observation or an annual-average route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter southward coastal branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 33,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"MONS\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian monsoon gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Equatorial Undercurrent - spring reference reach\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared53 E to91 E spring Indian EUC reference corridor. Longitude gates follow the reviewed 1963 observational domain; OSW chooses the equatorial line, connecting vertices and alternatives. Excludes Wyrtki surface jets, westward undercurrent conventions, anomalous fall episodes and whole-basin endpoints.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-thermocline eastward undercurrent geography. No uniform fixed depth reconstructed; 80.5 E, 50-150 m observations in 1994 are a different local occupation, not this route layer.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Spring eastward convention. Review reports several observations between 53 E and 91 E during March-April 1963; those stations do not establish a simultaneous continuous axis or annual recurrence.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"spring observational-domain reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf#page=29\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 50-90 E eastward winter surface reach. The 50 E start is an OSW offshore truncation beyond the western confluence, and 90 E follows approximate recirculation context. Neither is a diagnosed whole-current terminus. Excludes Somali/East African source legs, the southern return into SEC, South Java continuation, equatorial Wyrtki jets and subsurface SEUC.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source boreal winter December-March convention; Gauss-Markov seasonal climatology using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"December-March surface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"March-May subsurface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"monsoon\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Monsoon Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 77–83 E Sri Lanka regional summer reach, oriented eastward. Gates and connecting vertices are selected by OSW; neither gate is a physical whole-current endpoint. Excludes Arabian Sea source branches, Laccadive circulation, Bay of Bengal continuation, equatorial jets and subsurface counterflows. Different seasonal drawings do not diagnose occupied footprints or annual extrema.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Seasonal near-surface regional geography. Historical section evidence is shallow and depth dependent; no fixed-depth velocity axis reconstructed and undercurrents excluded.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Boreal summer source convention, June–September. Historical review and section context, not a simultaneous dated trajectory or current-year climatology.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"summer regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"monsoon\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Monsoon Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 77–83 E Sri Lanka regional winter reach, oriented westward. Gates and connecting vertices are selected by OSW; neither gate is a physical whole-current endpoint. Excludes Arabian Sea source branches, Laccadive circulation, Bay of Bengal continuation, equatorial jets and subsurface counterflows. Different seasonal drawings do not diagnose occupied footprints or annual extrema.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Seasonal near-surface regional geography. Historical section evidence is shallow and depth dependent; no fixed-depth velocity axis reconstructed and undercurrents excluded.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Boreal winter source convention, November–February. Historical review and section context, not a simultaneous dated trajectory or current-year climatology.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 4,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 4\r\n    },\r\n    \"IND E\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Eastern India coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"ISSG\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian South subtropical gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Source-scoped named-current extent from first clear evidence near 16 degrees E to loss of a recognizable jet between 66 and 70 degrees E. Does not include the subsequent South Indian Ocean Current or northern leakage branches.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Hydrographic frontal/jet geography; study geostrophic velocities referenced to 1500 m. No velocity axis extracted here.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source combines cruises over roughly twenty years, mostly austral summer; CTD data 1983–1991. The sketch is not a simultaneous or climatological observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"source-scoped extent route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 243,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 243,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Studied 21–60 degrees E reach only; excludes the western genesis and downstream termination. Not a whole-current length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Hydrographic frontal/jet geography; study geostrophic velocities referenced to 1500 m. No velocity axis extracted here.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source combines cruises over roughly twenty years, mostly austral summer; CTD data 1983–1991. The sketch is not a simultaneous or climatological observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"studied-reach reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-indian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Indian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Historical upper-1000 m geostrophic transport context, not a uniform-depth velocity axis or surface trajectory. Variable deep reference surfaces affect diagnosed transport; no layer-specific centerline reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial regional connection informed by historical hydrographic mean-flow context and source naming conventions. Not a simultaneous observation, monthly climatological axis or annual geometry.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"eastern regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"EAFR\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"East African coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional southward Agulhas reference route from 27 degrees S to a 40 degrees S retroflection gate near 19 degrees E. Includes an editorial approach to the turning region; stops before the eastward Agulhas Return Current. Excludes upstream Mozambique/East Madagascar branches, leakage and ring trajectories. This is a regional extent convention, not the narrower coastal-jet definition or whole Agulhas system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean current geography; no fixed depth or velocity axis extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial reference sketch, not an instantaneous or reanalysis mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"regional extent to retroflection\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.837906/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Source-scoped named-current extent from first clear evidence near 16 degrees E to loss of a recognizable jet between 66 and 70 degrees E. Does not include the subsequent South Indian Ocean Current or northern leakage branches.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Hydrographic frontal/jet geography; study geostrophic velocities referenced to 1500 m. No velocity axis extracted here.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source combines cruises over roughly twenty years, mostly austral summer; CTD data 1983–1991. The sketch is not a simultaneous or climatological observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"source-scoped extent route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 243,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 243,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Studied 21–60 degrees E reach only; excludes the western genesis and downstream termination. Not a whole-current length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Hydrographic frontal/jet geography; study geostrophic velocities referenced to 1500 m. No velocity axis extracted here.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source combines cruises over roughly twenty years, mostly austral summer; CTD data 1983–1991. The sketch is not a simultaneous or climatological observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"studied-reach reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Equatorial Undercurrent - spring reference reach\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared53 E to91 E spring Indian EUC reference corridor. Longitude gates follow the reviewed 1963 observational domain; OSW chooses the equatorial line, connecting vertices and alternatives. Excludes Wyrtki surface jets, westward undercurrent conventions, anomalous fall episodes and whole-basin endpoints.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-thermocline eastward undercurrent geography. No uniform fixed depth reconstructed; 80.5 E, 50-150 m observations in 1994 are a different local occupation, not this route layer.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Spring eastward convention. Review reports several observations between 53 E and 91 E during March-April 1963; those stations do not establish a simultaneous continuous axis or annual recurrence.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"spring observational-domain reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf#page=29\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 50-90 E eastward winter surface reach. The 50 E start is an OSW offshore truncation beyond the western confluence, and 90 E follows approximate recirculation context. Neither is a diagnosed whole-current terminus. Excludes Somali/East African source legs, the southern return into SEC, South Java continuation, equatorial Wyrtki jets and subsurface SEUC.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source boreal winter December-March convention; Gauss-Markov seasonal climatology using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"December-March surface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"March-May subsurface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Somali Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"June-July southern Somali coastal limb from an OSW equatorial gate northward to an OSW separation gate at 3.5 N. Source describes offshore departure south of 4 N and limited exchange with the northern Great Whirl. Excludes the upstream East African Coast Current, offshore Southern Gyre return limb, Great Whirl, Socotra outflow and undercurrents. This is one seasonal component, not the full summer Somali Current system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-layer southern seasonal coastal geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"June-July monsoon-onset two-gyre convention. Does not assume rare late-summer gyre coalescence or persistent whole-coast continuity.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"June-July southern coastal limb\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Somali Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northeast-monsoon southward Somali coastal branch from an OSW northern gate at 7 N to an OSW confluence gate at 3 S. Source latitude ranges are 6-8 N for divergence and 2-4 S for confluence with East African Coast Current. Excludes the northward flow north of the divergence, offshore feeder, eastward continuation, undercurrents and gyre circuits. No year-round whole-current extent asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface/upper-layer seasonal coastal reference geography; the source describes a shallow winter equatorial current, but no fixed-depth velocity axis is reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Northeast winter monsoon convention; not a simultaneous dated observation or an annual-average route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter southward coastal branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 6,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 6\r\n    },\r\n    \"AUSW\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Western Australian and Indonesian coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"BRAN2020 representative isopycnal context 27.9-28.7 sigma0. Source converts this to roughly 300-420 m at the mooring only; not a fixed-depth route throughout the basin.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"March-May monthly climatological context from 2001-2018 BRAN2020. Not a dated observed axis, annual geometry or a reconstruction of the anomalous 2020 current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"March-May subsurface studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"leeuwin-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"leeuwin\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Leeuwin Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Source-convention Leeuwin component from the North West Cape regional gate near 22 degrees S, southward around Cape Leeuwin and eastward into the central Great Australian Bight. Nominal eastern gate 130 degrees E uses the source's winter water-mass penetration convention; alternative 125 degrees E tests a shorter central-Bight naming convention. Excludes the North West Shelf, offshore eddies, South Australian and Zeehan components. Not the full 5,500 km boundary-flow system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Shelf-edge upper-ocean reference geography; no fixed-depth or diagnosed velocity axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial reference route under the source's autumn/winter southern-extension convention; not a simultaneous or climatological measured axis, nor a guaranteed summer path.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Leeuwin component into the Bight\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#leeuwin-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"ARCT\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic Arctic\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-greenland\",\r\n          \"name\": \"East Greenland Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional outer/slope EGC reference corridor from the Fram Strait section at 78.5 degrees N to the study’s southern shelf boundary at 59 degrees N in the Cape Farewell region. Excludes a distinct East Greenland Coastal Current axis, interior export branches, upstream Arctic extensions and onward West Greenland Current. The 59 degrees N gate is the paper’s regional boundary, not a precise geographic coordinate of Cape Farewell.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Outer/slope EGC geographic corridor only; no velocity layer, bathymetric axis or transport diagnosed. Separate from the near-surface coastal current.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General editorial reference corridor. The source analyzes VIKING20X and GLORYS12 during 1993–2019; this sketch is not their time-mean or instantaneous model axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"regional outer-EGC reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2023JC019890\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary regional continuation from the vicinity of 40 degrees N, 50 degrees W southeast of Grand Banks toward the western approaches of the British Isles. OSW chooses a nominal terminal gate west of Ireland, with southern/northern approach alternatives. Excludes Gulf Stream upstream, branches toward Iceland, the onward Norwegian/Canary flows and recirculation. A selected approach route is not the length of the entire branching Gulf Stream System.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean reference geography; no depth-specific velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial sketch under a glossary naming convention; not a synoptic path, parcel trajectory or climatological current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA North Atlantic regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 6,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"SARC\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic sub-Arctic\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-greenland-coastal\",\r\n          \"name\": \"East Greenland Coastal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared southeast Greenland coastal study-area reach from an OSW offshore gate near 66 N to a Cape Farewell offshore gate near 60 N. Excludes the weak northern 68 N identification, EGC shelfbreak path, Irminger Current, offshore diversions and West Greenland continuation. Not the full EGCC or the source-reported approximately 1000 km surveyed shelf. Near 63 N, the coastal and shelfbreak flows approach or merge; the line does not establish uninterrupted independent coastal flow. The local 30 km Cape Farewell width is not a buffer around this reach.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified low-salinity inner-shelf jet context from July-August 2004 hydrography and ADCP-referenced geostrophic velocity. No uniform fixed-depth axis diagnosed along this editorial path.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial regional geography informed by the July-August 2004 JR105 campaign. Not a simultaneous measured axis, annual mean or recurring summer footprint.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"66 N–Cape Farewell studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-greenland\",\r\n          \"name\": \"East Greenland Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional outer/slope EGC reference corridor from the Fram Strait section at 78.5 degrees N to the study’s southern shelf boundary at 59 degrees N in the Cape Farewell region. Excludes a distinct East Greenland Coastal Current axis, interior export branches, upstream Arctic extensions and onward West Greenland Current. The 59 degrees N gate is the paper’s regional boundary, not a precise geographic coordinate of Cape Farewell.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Outer/slope EGC geographic corridor only; no velocity layer, bathymetric axis or transport diagnosed. Separate from the near-surface coastal current.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General editorial reference corridor. The source analyzes VIKING20X and GLORYS12 during 1993–2019; this sketch is not their time-mean or instantaneous model axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"regional outer-EGC reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2023JC019890\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"irminger-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"irminger\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Irminger Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northward eastern-Irminger-Sea reference branch along the western Reykjanes Ridge flank, from an OSW southern ridge gate at 56 N to an OSW pre-bifurcation gate near 65 N south of Denmark Strait. Excludes return flow toward Greenland, North Icelandic Irminger continuation, interior Irminger Gyre circuits, offshore eddies, opposite East Reykjanes Ridge Current and deep overflow currents. Gates are regional comparison choices, not established whole-current endpoints.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-layer/surface-intensified regional branch geography. No fixed-depth or two-core velocity axis, ridge contour or deep-current route reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming convention supported by 2011 and 2026 source introductions; not a dated measured or modeled axis, annual average or water-parcel trajectory.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Irminger northward ridge-flank branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#irminger-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://rpickart.whoi.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/53/2016/02/DSR-The-Irminger-Gyre.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary regional continuation from the vicinity of 40 degrees N, 50 degrees W southeast of Grand Banks toward the western approaches of the British Isles. OSW chooses a nominal terminal gate west of Ireland, with southern/northern approach alternatives. Excludes Gulf Stream upstream, branches toward Iceland, the onward Norwegian/Canary flows and recirculation. A selected approach route is not the length of the entire branching Gulf Stream System.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean reference geography; no depth-specific velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial sketch under a glossary naming convention; not a synoptic path, parcel trajectory or climatological current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA North Atlantic regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"west-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"west-greenland\",\r\n          \"name\": \"West Greenland Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northward shelf-break West Greenland branch from an OSW Cape Farewell approach gate to an OSW Davis Strait gate near 67 N. Excludes the separate inshore West Greenland Coastal Current, the westward branch joining Labrador Current, shed Irminger Rings, fjords, upstream East Greenland/Irminger paths and continuation beyond the chosen Davis Strait gate. Not the whole bifurcating West Greenland Current system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Shelf-break regional reference geography. Source top-50 m mean model analysis supports pathway convention; no model velocity axis, common depth or 500 m isobath is extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional northward branch convention from Gou et al. (2022), whose model analysis covers 2008-2018. Drawn OSW route is not a measured/model-derived 2008-2018 axis or a simultaneous trajectory.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"West Greenland northward shelf-break branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#west-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC018404\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 63,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 5,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    \"NECS\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northeast Atlantic shelves\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"balearic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"balearic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Balearic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northern Balearic island-margin corridor from an OSW Ibiza offshore approach to a gate north/northeast of Menorca. Excludes upstream mainland Northern Current, its cyclonic return loop, southward channel flow, Algerian eddies and downstream basin recirculation. No full connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-layer current along Balearic shelf/slope naming context; no fixed-depth axis reconstructed. June 1989 survey described a roughly 250 m layer, not one width at all depths.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional island-margin reference informed by June 1989 FE-89 observations published in 1996 and 2020 model-comparison context. Not the actual cruise trajectory, annual mean axis, simultaneous observation or route valid through wind-driven reversals.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Balearic island-margin corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#balearic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00094/20507/18176.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"jutland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"jutland\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Jutland Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Danish west-coast reference corridor from an OSW German Bight approach gate to an offshore northern-Jutland/Skagerrak approach gate. Excludes upstream English Channel and southern North Sea circuits, Baltic Current inflow and Norwegian Coastal Current continuation. No North/South Jutland branch lengths or aliases admitted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional near-surface coastal naming context; not Atlantic bottom-water inflows or a reconstructed depth-specific core.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General regional circulation descriptions in 2015 and 2024 research papers. Not a contemporaneous trajectory, annual mean axis or seasonal route series; source sea-level seasonality is not a current-length measurement.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Danish-coast regional corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#jutland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2024.1416519/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary regional continuation from the vicinity of 40 degrees N, 50 degrees W southeast of Grand Banks toward the western approaches of the British Isles. OSW chooses a nominal terminal gate west of Ireland, with southern/northern approach alternatives. Excludes Gulf Stream upstream, branches toward Iceland, the onward Norwegian/Canary flows and recirculation. A selected approach route is not the length of the entire branching Gulf Stream System.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean reference geography; no depth-specific velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial sketch under a glossary naming convention; not a synoptic path, parcel trajectory or climatological current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA North Atlantic regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 78,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"northern-mediterranean\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Northern Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional Ligurian-to-Catalan Northern Current reference route ending at an OSW gate near the source-described 40.6 N bifurcation, with an earlier Catalan termination alternative. Excludes the Corsica feeder currents, downstream Ibiza and Balearic branches and offshore eddies. Exact gates and vertices are OSW choices; not the full western Mediterranean circulation.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-limb regional reference geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived current axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming convention from source introductions; not the two-week December 2011 Toulon survey trajectory or a simultaneous whole-route observation.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Ligurian-Catalan regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"norwegian-coastal\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Norwegian Coastal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW southern Norwegian Skagerrak approach to the Ingoy section at the Barents Sea entrance, following a simplified offshore coastal corridor. Excludes Baltic source-water transit, Jutland inflow, fjord circuits, offshore Norwegian Atlantic Current branches, West Spitsbergen and downstream Murman continuation. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Buoyant coastal-water naming context; no depth-specific core, full transverse section or uniform salinity footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography described by Christensen et al. (2026), with Ingoy context from Skagseth et al. (2011). Not a dated observed track, annual mean axis or seasonal geometry series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Norwegian coastal corridor to Ingoy\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/2785/2026/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 5,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    \"NWCS\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northwest Atlantic shelves\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"azores\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Azores Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW reference corridor from a Grand Banks branch-region gate near 40 N / 45 W, southeast to the Mid-Atlantic Ridge near 34 N / 37 W, then eastward toward an offshore Gulf of Cadiz approach gate. Excludes upstream Gulf Stream, North Atlantic branch, Azores Countercurrent, southern recirculation, southward branches into the North Equatorial/Canary routes and Gibraltar/Mediterranean inflow. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified eastward subtropical-jet naming context. Source long-term core analysis averages upper 1000 m; 2009 section samples deeper flow separately. No fixed-depth current axis or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography from Frazao et al. (2022), with 1993-1994 drifter and October-November 2009 section caveats. Selected vertices are neither the 1871-2010 model mean axis nor dated seasonal trajectories.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Azores eastward corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.842251/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"baffin-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"baffin\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Baffin Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Summer western-Baffin-Bay external coastal reference reach between OSW gates near the source-observed Lady Ann Strait latitude (76 N) and Cape Dyer latitude (67 N). Omits the Lancaster Sound intrusion and return, upstream Arctic strait feeders, transient eddies and continuation through southern Davis Strait. Source says at least these latitude limits; they are not whole-current endpoints. Exact offshore vertices are OSW choices, not a digitized observed trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Summer near-surface regional reach; source uses drifters, CTD and current meters at differing depths. No common-depth current axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Summer 1978/1979 geographic reach convention; editorial route does not represent one continuous observed dated trajectory or winter flow.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Baffin summer external coastal reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#baffin-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/63268.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"deep-western-boundary\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Deep Western Boundary Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"North Atlantic study-section reach from 47 degrees N to 24.5 degrees N via a coarse western-boundary reference corridor. Excludes upstream subpolar circulation, interior pathways, recirculation and tropical/South Atlantic continuation. Not the whole DWBC or a continuous observed deep-water pathway.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Source-defined deep circulation: around 2800 m to bottom at 47 degrees N, around 2682 m to bottom at 36 degrees N, and around 2500–5500 m at 24.5 degrees N. Interfaces vary by section; no common fixed-depth axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route linking source section latitudes; not a simultaneous measured trajectory or a 1990–2019 mean current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Atlantic studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"gaspe-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"gaspe\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Gaspé Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW southern lower-estuary offshore approach near Pointe-des-Monts latitude, along the Gaspe Peninsula and toward a gate north of the Magdalen Islands. Excludes upstream river/estuary length, episodic north-shore feeder, Anticosti Gyre circuit, Chaleur Bay recirculation and Cabot Strait/Scotian downstream routes. No full connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-layer coastal jet naming context; typical regional summary describes approximately upper 40 m. No depth-specific velocity core or uniform transverse footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional reference informed by February 2022 thesis introduction and a 2024 coastal circulation-model description. Not a dated observed path, annual mean axis or continuous trajectory through all meanders and detachments.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Gaspe regional coastal corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#gaspe-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://semaphore.uqar.ca/2055/1/Theau_Leclercq_fevrier2022.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"labrador-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"labrador\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Labrador Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Main offshore Labrador regional branch from an OSW southern Davis Strait gate at 60 N, along Labrador and east Newfoundland, via the western Flemish Pass region to an OSW tail-of-Grand-Banks gate at 43 N. Excludes upstream Baffin/West Greenland feeder paths, Hudson Strait intrusion, inshore Avalon branch, offshore eddy excursions and downstream westward/eastward branches. Source defines regions, not exact gates or a whole-system termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean offshore branch geography; no fixed-depth, velocity-derived core or deep western boundary axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming convention from a 1984 government synthesis; not a simultaneous observation, dated model field or assertion of constant current strength.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Labrador main offshore regional branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#labrador-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/Library/40621704.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary regional continuation from the vicinity of 40 degrees N, 50 degrees W southeast of Grand Banks toward the western approaches of the British Isles. OSW chooses a nominal terminal gate west of Ireland, with southern/northern approach alternatives. Excludes Gulf Stream upstream, branches toward Iceland, the onward Norwegian/Canary flows and recirculation. A selected approach route is not the length of the entire branching Gulf Stream System.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean reference geography; no depth-specific velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial sketch under a glossary naming convention; not a synoptic path, parcel trajectory or climatological current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA North Atlantic regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"west-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"west-greenland\",\r\n          \"name\": \"West Greenland Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northward shelf-break West Greenland branch from an OSW Cape Farewell approach gate to an OSW Davis Strait gate near 67 N. Excludes the separate inshore West Greenland Coastal Current, the westward branch joining Labrador Current, shed Irminger Rings, fjords, upstream East Greenland/Irminger paths and continuation beyond the chosen Davis Strait gate. Not the whole bifurcating West Greenland Current system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Shelf-break regional reference geography. Source top-50 m mean model analysis supports pathway convention; no model velocity axis, common depth or 500 m isobath is extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional northward branch convention from Gou et al. (2022), whose model analysis covers 2008-2018. Drawn OSW route is not a measured/model-derived 2008-2018 axis or a simultaneous trajectory.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"West Greenland northward shelf-break branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#west-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022JC018404\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 7,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 7\r\n    },\r\n    \"NADR\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"North Atlantic Drift\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"azores\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Azores Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW reference corridor from a Grand Banks branch-region gate near 40 N / 45 W, southeast to the Mid-Atlantic Ridge near 34 N / 37 W, then eastward toward an offshore Gulf of Cadiz approach gate. Excludes upstream Gulf Stream, North Atlantic branch, Azores Countercurrent, southern recirculation, southward branches into the North Equatorial/Canary routes and Gibraltar/Mediterranean inflow. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified eastward subtropical-jet naming context. Source long-term core analysis averages upper 1000 m; 2009 section samples deeper flow separately. No fixed-depth current axis or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography from Frazao et al. (2022), with 1993-1994 drifter and October-November 2009 section caveats. Selected vertices are neither the 1871-2010 model mean axis nor dated seasonal trajectories.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Azores eastward corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.842251/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"deep-western-boundary\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Deep Western Boundary Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"North Atlantic study-section reach from 47 degrees N to 24.5 degrees N via a coarse western-boundary reference corridor. Excludes upstream subpolar circulation, interior pathways, recirculation and tropical/South Atlantic continuation. Not the whole DWBC or a continuous observed deep-water pathway.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Source-defined deep circulation: around 2800 m to bottom at 47 degrees N, around 2682 m to bottom at 36 degrees N, and around 2500–5500 m at 24.5 degrees N. Interfaces vary by section; no common fixed-depth axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route linking source section latitudes; not a simultaneous measured trajectory or a 1990–2019 mean current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Atlantic studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 9,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"NOAA glossary regional continuation from the vicinity of 40 degrees N, 50 degrees W southeast of Grand Banks toward the western approaches of the British Isles. OSW chooses a nominal terminal gate west of Ireland, with southern/northern approach alternatives. Excludes Gulf Stream upstream, branches toward Iceland, the onward Norwegian/Canary flows and recirculation. A selected approach route is not the length of the entire branching Gulf Stream System.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean reference geography; no depth-specific velocity axis diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial sketch under a glossary naming convention; not a synoptic path, parcel trajectory or climatological current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"NOAA North Atlantic regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"portugal\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Portugal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW offshore reference corridor from a selected gate within the 45-50 N North Atlantic/Azores interface region to a selected 35 N Canary feed-region gate. Excludes Portugal Coastal Current, Portugal Coastal Countercurrent, slope undercurrents, Azores eastward jet and downstream Canary route. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface offshore southward-flow naming context; 2002 drifters had drogues at 15 m. No depth-specific core or full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional circulation geography from an undated repository chapter, 1993-1994 observations published in 2002, and a 2026 regional synthesis. Selected route is not a dated trajectory or annual/seasonal mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Portugal offshore corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers12-12/010038152.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 4,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"GFST\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Gulf Stream\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"deep-western-boundary\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Deep Western Boundary Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"North Atlantic study-section reach from 47 degrees N to 24.5 degrees N via a coarse western-boundary reference corridor. Excludes upstream subpolar circulation, interior pathways, recirculation and tropical/South Atlantic continuation. Not the whole DWBC or a continuous observed deep-water pathway.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Source-defined deep circulation: around 2800 m to bottom at 47 degrees N, around 2682 m to bottom at 36 degrees N, and around 2500–5500 m at 24.5 degrees N. Interfaces vary by section; no common fixed-depth axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route linking source section latitudes; not a simultaneous measured trajectory or a 1990–2019 mean current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Atlantic studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"NAST E\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northeast Atlantic subtropical gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"azores\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Azores Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW reference corridor from a Grand Banks branch-region gate near 40 N / 45 W, southeast to the Mid-Atlantic Ridge near 34 N / 37 W, then eastward toward an offshore Gulf of Cadiz approach gate. Excludes upstream Gulf Stream, North Atlantic branch, Azores Countercurrent, southern recirculation, southward branches into the North Equatorial/Canary routes and Gibraltar/Mediterranean inflow. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified eastward subtropical-jet naming context. Source long-term core analysis averages upper 1000 m; 2009 section samples deeper flow separately. No fixed-depth current axis or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography from Frazao et al. (2022), with 1993-1994 drifter and October-November 2009 section caveats. Selected vertices are neither the 1871-2010 model mean axis nor dated seasonal trajectories.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Azores eastward corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.842251/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"portugal\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Portugal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW offshore reference corridor from a selected gate within the 45-50 N North Atlantic/Azores interface region to a selected 35 N Canary feed-region gate. Excludes Portugal Coastal Current, Portugal Coastal Countercurrent, slope undercurrents, Azores eastward jet and downstream Canary route. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface offshore southward-flow naming context; 2002 drifters had drogues at 15 m. No depth-specific core or full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional circulation geography from an undated repository chapter, 1993-1994 observations published in 2002, and a 2026 regional synthesis. Selected route is not a dated trajectory or annual/seasonal mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Portugal offshore corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers12-12/010038152.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"NAST W\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Northwest Atlantic subtropical gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"azores\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Azores Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW reference corridor from a Grand Banks branch-region gate near 40 N / 45 W, southeast to the Mid-Atlantic Ridge near 34 N / 37 W, then eastward toward an offshore Gulf of Cadiz approach gate. Excludes upstream Gulf Stream, North Atlantic branch, Azores Countercurrent, southern recirculation, southward branches into the North Equatorial/Canary routes and Gibraltar/Mediterranean inflow. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified eastward subtropical-jet naming context. Source long-term core analysis averages upper 1000 m; 2009 section samples deeper flow separately. No fixed-depth current axis or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography from Frazao et al. (2022), with 1993-1994 drifter and October-November 2009 section caveats. Selected vertices are neither the 1871-2010 model mean axis nor dated seasonal trajectories.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Azores eastward corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.842251/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 66,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"MEDI\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Mediterranean Sea\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"algerian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"algerian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Algerian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Eastward Algerian coastal regional reference route from an OSW Alboran-transition gate to an OSW eastern Algeria gate. Alternative later western and earlier eastern gates test regional extent. Excludes Alboran gyres, detached Algerian eddies and downstream Sardinia-channel or other Mediterranean circulation. Source does not define exact terminal coordinates or whole-system termination.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface Atlantic Water regional coastal reference geography; no velocity-derived current axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional source-description convention; not a complete observed trajectory from the 2014-2016 glider surveys.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Algerian coastal regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#algerian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://essd.copernicus.org/articles/11/147/2019/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 108,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 108,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"balearic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"balearic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Balearic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northern Balearic island-margin corridor from an OSW Ibiza offshore approach to a gate north/northeast of Menorca. Excludes upstream mainland Northern Current, its cyclonic return loop, southward channel flow, Algerian eddies and downstream basin recirculation. No full connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-layer current along Balearic shelf/slope naming context; no fixed-depth axis reconstructed. June 1989 survey described a roughly 250 m layer, not one width at all depths.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional island-margin reference informed by June 1989 FE-89 observations published in 1996 and 2020 model-comparison context. Not the actual cruise trajectory, annual mean axis, simultaneous observation or route valid through wind-driven reversals.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Balearic island-margin corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#balearic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00094/20507/18176.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"east-adriatic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"East Adriatic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW offshore eastern-Adriatic reference corridor under the Otranto-to-Istria surface-circulation convention. Gates are editorial neighborhoods, not observed origins or termination. Excludes western return flow, sub-basin recirculation loops and unverified island-channel branches. The possible Dalmatian-name overlap is unresolved and its extent is not transferred. The published 800 km basin length is not used as current length; this estimate comes from the declared OSW vertices.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"General surface-circulation geography; no velocity-defined current core or uniform intermediate/full-depth layer diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial corridor supported by published general circulation descriptions. Not the 2002-2003 local mooring trajectory, annual mean observed axis or seasonal path.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Otranto-Istria surface-circulation convention\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"ligurian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Ligurian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared coastal studied reach of the Northern Current from an OSW offshore Genoa neighborhood gate through the Imperia sector to an OSW Menton–Nice neighborhood gate. Ligurian is retained as the ledger regional segment classification, not a separate additive current system. Excludes Corsica feeder routes, basin-wide drifter loops and downstream Provencal/Catalan continuation. Gates are not whole-current endpoints.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-flow geography in a study combining CODE drifters following the first metre and ARGOSPHERE drifters following the first 10–20 cm with unquantified wind slip. No full-depth or shelf-break axis diagnosed from the editorial route.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source drifter sampling is intermittent during May–October 2007 and October 2008–January 2009. The selected reach is editorial geographic context, not one float trajectory, simultaneous observation, annual mean or seasonal path.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"coastal Genoa–Nice studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#ligurian-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"northern-mediterranean\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Northern Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional Ligurian-to-Catalan Northern Current reference route ending at an OSW gate near the source-described 40.6 N bifurcation, with an earlier Catalan termination alternative. Excludes the Corsica feeder currents, downstream Ibiza and Balearic branches and offshore eddies. Exact gates and vertices are OSW choices; not the full western Mediterranean circulation.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-limb regional reference geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived current axis.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming convention from source introductions; not the two-week December 2011 Toulon survey trajectory or a simultaneous whole-route observation.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Ligurian-Catalan regional route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"western-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"western-adriatic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Western Adriatic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Po-region offshore approach to western Otranto along the Italian Adriatic coast. Regional surface route, not the whole vertically structured western Adriatic circulation. Excludes eastern boundary inflow, cross-basin gyre circuits, Gulf of Manfredonia recirculation, deep dense-water pathways and downstream Ionian continuation.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface coastal corridor. No bottom/slope dense-water branch or fixed-depth velocity core reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional surface naming convention informed by 1990-2007 drifter context and 2018 regional synthesis. Not a simultaneous drifter trajectory, annual mean axis or route valid during every wind reversal.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Italian-coast surface corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#western-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/9/713/2013/os-9-713-2013.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 6,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 6\r\n    },\r\n    \"CNRY\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Canary Current coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"azores\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Azores Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW reference corridor from a Grand Banks branch-region gate near 40 N / 45 W, southeast to the Mid-Atlantic Ridge near 34 N / 37 W, then eastward toward an offshore Gulf of Cadiz approach gate. Excludes upstream Gulf Stream, North Atlantic branch, Azores Countercurrent, southern recirculation, southward branches into the North Equatorial/Canary routes and Gibraltar/Mediterranean inflow. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface-intensified eastward subtropical-jet naming context. Source long-term core analysis averages upper 1000 m; 2009 section samples deeper flow separately. No fixed-depth current axis or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography from Frazao et al. (2022), with 1993-1994 drifter and October-November 2009 section caveats. Selected vertices are neither the 1871-2010 model mean axis nor dated seasonal trajectories.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Azores eastward corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.842251/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"canary-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"canary\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Canary Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW offshore reference corridor from a regional northern source gate near 35 N, past the western Canary archipelago, to a Cape Blanc offshore departure gate near 21 N. Excludes upstream Azores/Portugal routes, the broader Iberian-to-tropical Canary Current System, Lanzarote Passage recirculation, poleward undercurrents and downstream North Equatorial Current. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean southward return-flow naming context; source descriptions mention central waters over approximately upper 200-300 m. No depth-specific velocity core or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional circulation geography from 2018/2026 papers, with seasonal-path caveats from 2015 observations published in 2023. Selected offshore corridor is not a dated trajectory, annual mean axis or a particular seasonal route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Canary offshore return-flow corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#canary-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/971/2018/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"mauritanian-summer-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"mauritanian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Mauritanian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 17 N to 20 N offshore Mauritanian summer surface reference reach south of Cap Blanc (21 N). OSW selects both regional truncation gates and offshore vertices. Excludes bank circulation, Canary equatorward upwelling jet and the subsurface winter continuation toward Cape Bojador; not complete current endpoints.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Summer surface poleward circulation geography; no fixed-depth velocity axis or physical width extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source summer surface-flow convention south of Cap Blanc, without an explicit month window in this passage. Winter flow is subsurface; no winter surface counterpart or annual geometry is asserted.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Mauritanian summer surface reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#mauritanian-summer-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://ocg.aori.u-tokyo.ac.jp/member/eoka/documents/Tomczak_Godfrey.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"mediterranean-undercurrent-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"mediterranean-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Mediterranean Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared southwestern Iberian lower-core reach from the AMUSE launch neighborhood near 8.5 W, 36.5 N, westward around Cape St. Vincent and northward to an OSW western-slope gate at 38.2 N near the Lisbon/Setubal canyon region. Excludes upstream Gibraltar gravity-current descent, offshore Mediterranean Water spreading, meddy looping, Estremadura branch dynamics and uncertain farther-north continuity. Not a full-current axis or float trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Nonmeddy lower-core Mediterranean Water context, 950–1250 dbar observational selection. Pressure bounds are not converted to uniform depth; vertically separated cores and upstream bottom-trapped density flow remain distinct.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"AMUSE floats deployed May 1993–March 1994 and tracked for up to 11 months, with May 1993 hydrography and augmented Iberian observations. Selected path is editorial geography, not one dated float trajectory, annual mean or seasonal axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"SW Iberian lower-core studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#mediterranean-undercurrent-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2001JC001007\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"portugal\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Portugal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW offshore reference corridor from a selected gate within the 45-50 N North Atlantic/Azores interface region to a selected 35 N Canary feed-region gate. Excludes Portugal Coastal Current, Portugal Coastal Countercurrent, slope undercurrents, Azores eastward jet and downstream Canary route. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface offshore southward-flow naming context; 2002 drifters had drogues at 15 m. No depth-specific core or full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional circulation geography from an undated repository chapter, 1993-1994 observations published in 2002, and a 2026 regional synthesis. Selected route is not a dated trajectory or annual/seasonal mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Portugal offshore corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/divers12-12/010038152.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 5,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    \"NATR\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"North Atlantic tropical gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"CARB\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Caribbean\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"antilles-northern-bahamas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"antilles\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Antilles Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Conditional regional reference from OSW 26.5 N offshore-Abaco gate to OSW 28 N northwestward approach gate north of Little Bahama Bank. Both gates and all bends are editorial regional truncations, not observed current origins, terminations or a Gulf Stream junction. Southern Antilles, Florida Current, Gulf Stream, DWBC and eddy loops excluded.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Modern mean-flow naming context in the upper 1000 dbar with a subsurface peak near 400 dbar at 26.5 N. No fixed-pressure axis or depth-following trajectory diagnosed. Pressure is not converted to metres; NASA surface animation is only geographic context.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated conditional editorial connection around northern Bahamas. Meinen 2005-2015 mean evidence is local to 26.5 N; it does not date this full path. KN-200-4 (13 April-3 May 2011) did not detect the characteristic Antilles Current off Abaco while finding north-bank westward flow; these are not asserted to be one continuous observed current.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"conditional northern Bahamas reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#antilles-northern-bahamas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/20909/noaa_20909_DS1.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"caribbean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"caribbean\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Caribbean Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Selected westward Caribbean regional route from a Windward Islands approach to the Belize/Yucatan transition near 19 N. Excludes the northward Yucatan Current, Loop and Florida currents, additional island entry branches, Colombia-Panama gyre circuits and eddy perimeters. No unique continuous axis or whole-system length asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface regional geography; no fixed-depth velocity axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional convention informed by 1996-2001 near-surface drifter circulation; not a dated trajectory or extracted mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Caribbean regional corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#caribbean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2002GL016231\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"deep-western-boundary\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Deep Western Boundary Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"North Atlantic study-section reach from 47 degrees N to 24.5 degrees N via a coarse western-boundary reference corridor. Excludes upstream subpolar circulation, interior pathways, recirculation and tropical/South Atlantic continuation. Not the whole DWBC or a continuous observed deep-water pathway.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Source-defined deep circulation: around 2800 m to bottom at 47 degrees N, around 2682 m to bottom at 36 degrees N, and around 2500–5500 m at 24.5 degrees N. Interfaces vary by section; no common fixed-depth axis reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route linking source section latitudes; not a simultaneous measured trajectory or a 1990–2019 mean current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Atlantic studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"GUIA\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Guianas coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 42 W to 32 W western summer study reach: one editor-selected NECC connection inside the source regional surface-flow context. Branch assignment and joining remain review gates. Excludes independent northern-branch geometry, upstream NBC retroflection, equatorial ESC and eastern-basin continuation. Not a whole-current length or sum of branches. All latitude gates and bends are editorial.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Altimetry-derived surface geostrophic context; no fixed-depth velocity core, parcel trajectory or depth-uniform axis inferred.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route guided by the 1993-2017 boreal-summer climatological context (July-August-September). Not a dated axis, monthly mean measured centerline or year-round route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"42 W to 32 W western summer study reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/251/2023/os-19-251-2023.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 18,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"guiana-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"guiana\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Guiana Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional Guianas survey-domain corridor from an offshore Maroni approach through the Demerara and Orinoco approaches to east of Trinidad. Both endpoints and all vertices are OSW geographic choices within the report's regional context, not named-current origins, terminations or measured station positions. Excludes a whole North Brazil Current, Caribbean continuation, offshore retroflection, ring trajectories and river-plume boundaries.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional current geography. No fixed-depth, depth-averaged or direct velocity axis is reconstructed; deeper counterflow and freshwater bands are not this route.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Geographic context from a report of four repeated hydrographic surveys in 1988, published November 1989. This route is not an observed 1988 trajectory, seasonal axis, annual mean or modern operational current position.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Guianas survey-domain regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#guiana-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.fao.org/4/x6078e/x6078e03.htm\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-brazil\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Brazil Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northwestward surface North Brazil regional branch from an OSW gate near the source-described 5 S origin to a nominal 7 N retroflection approach. Alternative terminal conventions stop at 5 or 9 N. Excludes upstream North Brazil Undercurrent, offshore retroflected return branch, NECC/EUC continuations, Guiana continuation and detached ring tracks or perimeters. No whole circulation-system length asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface/upper-layer regional geography after the upstream undercurrent surfaces; no fixed-depth core or velocity contour extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional surface naming and retroflection gate conventions; not a dated axis, annual average or model-derived seasonal length distribution.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Brazil surface branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/251/2023/os-19-251-2023.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"WTRA\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Western tropical Atlantic\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared Atlantic equatorial subsurface-jet reach from the 35 W observational section to an OSW 5 E pre-island approach gate. Excludes western North Brazil retroflection source paths, island bifurcation near 6 E, downstream branches and westward returns. Not full source-to-termination length or an observed material trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface equatorial/thermocline jet. At 35 W the reported mean observed core is about 100 m; eastern cores and isopycnal layers differ. No single depth is imposed on the route; surface SEC/NECC and deeper equatorial currents remain separate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial geographic reach using Hormann and Brandt (2007) observations/model comparison and Napolitano et al. (2022) eastern-island study. Composite periods differ; no single dated or annual mean axis or seasonal geometry series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"35 W to pre-island equatorial reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2022-11/010086132.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 42 W to 32 W western summer study reach: one editor-selected NECC connection inside the source regional surface-flow context. Branch assignment and joining remain review gates. Excludes independent northern-branch geometry, upstream NBC retroflection, equatorial ESC and eastern-basin continuation. Not a whole-current length or sum of branches. All latitude gates and bends are editorial.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Altimetry-derived surface geostrophic context; no fixed-depth velocity core, parcel trajectory or depth-uniform axis inferred.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial route guided by the 1993-2017 boreal-summer climatological context (July-August-September). Not a dated axis, monthly mean measured centerline or year-round route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"42 W to 32 W western summer study reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-necc-western-summer-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/251/2023/os-19-251-2023.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central Atlantic subsurface reference reach between observations at 35 W near 5 N and the central observational neighborhood at 23 W near 5 N. Connecting vertices are editorial, not an observed continuous axis. Excludes NBC/NEC source recirculation, surface NECC flow, uncertain filaments east of 28 W and farther-east termination. Not full-current source-to-end length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface eastward NEUC context. The central mooring study defines 65–270 m; historical western cores lie near sigma-theta 26.75 kg/m3. These different vertical definitions are not imposed as one uniform layer along the reference line.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Western sections in February 1993 and April 1996; central moorings June 2006–February 2008 and November 2009–January 2018 with 2002–2018 ship sections. Editorial section-to-section geography, not simultaneous observations or an annual/seasonal axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"35 W–23 W subsurface reference reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central Atlantic subsurface reach from the 35 W section near 3 S to an OSW truncation near 10 W, 4.3 S. Uses the published float-study domain, not full-current start and termination. Excludes westward SEC legs, NBUC source pathways, recirculation loops, surface drift and uncertain central/eastern continuation.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface eastward flow in the context of floats parked at 200 m. The 200 m level is sampling support, not a uniform core depth or full vertical extent. Ship-section 100–500 m and density-defined transport integrations are separate diagnostics.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Float deployments in 2000–2004 and 2004–2006; ship-section composites span 1990–2008. Editorial geographic reach is not one observed float trajectory, dated axis, annual mean or seasonal series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"200 m context western-to-central studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008GL035753\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"brazil\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Brazil Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Poleward Brazil Current reference route from nominal 14 degrees S origin to nominal 38 degrees S confluence; alternate origins 10/15 degrees S and terminal proxies 34.5/40.5 degrees S. Excludes North Brazil Current, Brazil Return Current recirculation, eastward South Atlantic Current and deep intermediate undercurrent. Confluence-proxy positions are endpoint assumptions, not instantaneous observed axes.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean poleward BC branch geographic reference only. No fixed vertical interval or undercurrent route diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General geographic sketch using source-described origin and confluence variability. Neither the 2009–2015 mooring period nor the front proxy interval creates a contemporaneous full-current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"poleward-branch reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020JC017146\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": false,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 9,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-brazil\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Brazil Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Northwestward surface North Brazil regional branch from an OSW gate near the source-described 5 S origin to a nominal 7 N retroflection approach. Alternative terminal conventions stop at 5 or 9 N. Excludes upstream North Brazil Undercurrent, offshore retroflected return branch, NECC/EUC continuations, Guiana continuation and detached ring tracks or perimeters. No whole circulation-system length asserted.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Surface/upper-layer regional geography after the upstream undercurrent surfaces; no fixed-depth core or velocity contour extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional surface naming and retroflection gate conventions; not a dated axis, annual average or model-derived seasonal length distribution.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"North Brazil surface branch\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/251/2023/os-19-251-2023.html\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 6,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    \"ETRA\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Eastern tropical Atlantic\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared Atlantic equatorial subsurface-jet reach from the 35 W observational section to an OSW 5 E pre-island approach gate. Excludes western North Brazil retroflection source paths, island bifurcation near 6 E, downstream branches and westward returns. Not full source-to-termination length or an observed material trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface equatorial/thermocline jet. At 35 W the reported mean observed core is about 100 m; eastern cores and isopycnal layers differ. No single depth is imposed on the route; surface SEC/NECC and deeper equatorial currents remain separate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial geographic reach using Hormann and Brandt (2007) observations/model comparison and Napolitano et al. (2022) eastern-island study. Composite periods differ; no single dated or annual mean axis or seasonal geometry series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"35 W to pre-island equatorial reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2022-11/010086132.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western-to-central Atlantic subsurface reach from the 35 W section near 3 S to an OSW truncation near 10 W, 4.3 S. Uses the published float-study domain, not full-current start and termination. Excludes westward SEC legs, NBUC source pathways, recirculation loops, surface drift and uncertain central/eastern continuation.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface eastward flow in the context of floats parked at 200 m. The 200 m level is sampling support, not a uniform core depth or full vertical extent. Ship-section 100–500 m and density-defined transport integrations are separate diagnostics.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Float deployments in 2000–2004 and 2004–2006; ship-section composites span 1990–2008. Editorial geographic reach is not one observed float trajectory, dated axis, annual mean or seasonal series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"200 m context western-to-central studied reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-seuc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2008GL035753\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"guinea-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"guinea\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Guinea Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Cape Palmas offshore approach to the Togo-Benin weakening transition near 2 E. Regional route convention, not the full Guinea Current extent. Excludes upstream equatorial countercurrent, Guinea Counter Current, Guinea Under Current, plume recirculation and eddy excursions.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface regional geography; source describes Guinea Current in upper 50 m. No fixed-depth velocity core reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Summer regional convention informed by 2010-2017 model climatology and 1979-2019 drifter climatology; not a digitized seasonal mean axis or annual mean length.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Guinea regional near-surface route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#guinea-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.607216/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"GUIN\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Guinea Current coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared Atlantic equatorial subsurface-jet reach from the 35 W observational section to an OSW 5 E pre-island approach gate. Excludes western North Brazil retroflection source paths, island bifurcation near 6 E, downstream branches and westward returns. Not full source-to-termination length or an observed material trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Subsurface equatorial/thermocline jet. At 35 W the reported mean observed core is about 100 m; eastern cores and isopycnal layers differ. No single depth is imposed on the route; surface SEC/NECC and deeper equatorial currents remain separate.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial geographic reach using Hormann and Brandt (2007) observations/model comparison and Napolitano et al. (2022) eastern-island study. Composite periods differ; no single dated or annual mean axis or seasonal geometry series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"35 W to pre-island equatorial reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#atlantic-euc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/2022-11/010086132.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"guinea-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"guinea\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Guinea Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Cape Palmas offshore approach to the Togo-Benin weakening transition near 2 E. Regional route convention, not the full Guinea Current extent. Excludes upstream equatorial countercurrent, Guinea Counter Current, Guinea Under Current, plume recirculation and eddy excursions.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Near-surface regional geography; source describes Guinea Current in upper 50 m. No fixed-depth velocity core reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Summer regional convention informed by 2010-2017 model climatology and 1979-2019 drifter climatology; not a digitized seasonal mean axis or annual mean length.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Guinea regional near-surface route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#guinea-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2020.607216/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"SATL\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"South Atlantic gyre\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western intermediate-depth SAC reference reach from a 40 W, 39 S current-center context gate to the 16 W, 43 S Mid-Atlantic Ridge float-reach context gate. Excludes upstream Brazil/Falkland confluence paths, unresolved eastern-basin continuation and recirculation. Not a complete current or a digitized float trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Intermediate/Antarctic Intermediate Water context from subsurface floats; no velocity core, exact isopycnal or uniform-depth axis reconstructed. Surface STF geography does not replace this layer scope.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Study observations span December 1992–October 1996; selected route is an editorial geographic reach, not a time-mean axis, dated trajectory or seasonal curve.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"western intermediate SAC reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.aoml.noaa.gov/phod/docs/boebel_et_al1999a.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"BRAZ\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Brazil Current coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"brazil\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Brazil Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Poleward Brazil Current reference route from nominal 14 degrees S origin to nominal 38 degrees S confluence; alternate origins 10/15 degrees S and terminal proxies 34.5/40.5 degrees S. Excludes North Brazil Current, Brazil Return Current recirculation, eastward South Atlantic Current and deep intermediate undercurrent. Confluence-proxy positions are endpoint assumptions, not instantaneous observed axes.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean poleward BC branch geographic reference only. No fixed vertical interval or undercurrent route diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General geographic sketch using source-described origin and confluence variability. Neither the 2009–2015 mooring period nor the front proxy interval creates a contemporaneous full-current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"poleward-branch reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020JC017146\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-atlantic\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Atlantic Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western intermediate-depth SAC reference reach from a 40 W, 39 S current-center context gate to the 16 W, 43 S Mid-Atlantic Ridge float-reach context gate. Excludes upstream Brazil/Falkland confluence paths, unresolved eastern-basin continuation and recirculation. Not a complete current or a digitized float trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Intermediate/Antarctic Intermediate Water context from subsurface floats; no velocity core, exact isopycnal or uniform-depth axis reconstructed. Surface STF geography does not replace this layer scope.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Study observations span December 1992–October 1996; selected route is an editorial geographic reach, not a time-mean axis, dated trajectory or seasonal curve.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"western intermediate SAC reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.aoml.noaa.gov/phod/docs/boebel_et_al1999a.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 2,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 2\r\n    },\r\n    \"BENG\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Benguela Current coast\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"benguela-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"benguela\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Benguela Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Specified northward shelf-edge Benguela regional reference branch from an offshore Cape Agulhas regional gate to the nominal 15 degrees S Angola–Benguela front region. Excludes broad offshore Benguela extensions, Agulhas ring paths, southward undercurrent and the entire upwelling-ecosystem perimeter. Gate coordinates are OSW regional approximations; no continuous measured shelf-edge axis is inferred.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Northward shelf-edge branch reference geography; no fixed velocity layer diagnosed. Distinct from offshore/underlying circulation.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General editorial reference sketch; combines regional source descriptions, not a simultaneous 1997 or decadal inverse-model current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"shelf-edge branch reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#benguela-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"FKLD\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Southwest Atlantic shelves\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"brazil\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Brazil Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Poleward Brazil Current reference route from nominal 14 degrees S origin to nominal 38 degrees S confluence; alternate origins 10/15 degrees S and terminal proxies 34.5/40.5 degrees S. Excludes North Brazil Current, Brazil Return Current recirculation, eastward South Atlantic Current and deep intermediate undercurrent. Confluence-proxy positions are endpoint assumptions, not instantaneous observed axes.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean poleward BC branch geographic reference only. No fixed vertical interval or undercurrent route diagnosed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General geographic sketch using source-described origin and confluence variability. Neither the 2009–2015 mooring period nor the front proxy interval creates a contemporaneous full-current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"poleward-branch reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2020JC017146\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 18,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": false\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"SSTC\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"South subtropical convergence\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Regional southward Agulhas reference route from 27 degrees S to a 40 degrees S retroflection gate near 19 degrees E. Includes an editorial approach to the turning region; stops before the eastward Agulhas Return Current. Excludes upstream Mozambique/East Madagascar branches, leakage and ring trajectories. This is a regional extent convention, not the narrower coastal-jet definition or whole Agulhas system.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Regional upper-ocean current geography; no fixed depth or velocity axis extracted.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Undated editorial reference sketch, not an instantaneous or reanalysis mean axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"regional extent to retroflection\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2022.837906/full\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Source-scoped named-current extent from first clear evidence near 16 degrees E to loss of a recognizable jet between 66 and 70 degrees E. Does not include the subsequent South Indian Ocean Current or northern leakage branches.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Hydrographic frontal/jet geography; study geostrophic velocities referenced to 1500 m. No velocity axis extracted here.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source combines cruises over roughly twenty years, mostly austral summer; CTD data 1983–1991. The sketch is not a simultaneous or climatological observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"source-scoped extent route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 243,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 243,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Studied 21–60 degrees E reach only; excludes the western genesis and downstream termination. Not a whole-current length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Hydrographic frontal/jet geography; study geostrophic velocities referenced to 1500 m. No velocity axis extracted here.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Source combines cruises over roughly twenty years, mostly austral summer; CTD data 1983–1991. The sketch is not a simultaneous or climatological observed centerline.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"studied-reach reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"benguela-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"benguela\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Benguela Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Specified northward shelf-edge Benguela regional reference branch from an offshore Cape Agulhas regional gate to the nominal 15 degrees S Angola–Benguela front region. Excludes broad offshore Benguela extensions, Agulhas ring paths, southward undercurrent and the entire upwelling-ecosystem perimeter. Gate coordinates are OSW regional approximations; no continuous measured shelf-edge axis is inferred.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Northward shelf-edge branch reference geography; no fixed velocity layer diagnosed. Distinct from offshore/underlying circulation.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"General editorial reference sketch; combines regional source descriptions, not a simultaneous 1997 or decadal inverse-model current axis.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"shelf-edge branch reference route\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#benguela-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/1009/2023/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    },\r\n    \"SANT\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Subantarctic water ring\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-indian\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Indian Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared 70 E to 90 E eastern-name-convention regional reach. The west gate follows the later convention reserving South Indian Ocean Current for flow beyond the Agulhas Return Current near 70 E; the east gate is the approximate recirculation/splitting region described in historical hydrography. These are selected regional gates, not whole-current endpoints. Western Agulhas Return, northward recirculation, northeastern Australia continuation and ACC paths are not added. All route latitudes and connecting vertices are editorial.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Historical upper-1000 m geostrophic transport context, not a uniform-depth velocity axis or surface trajectory. Variable deep reference surfaces affect diagnosed transport; no layer-specific centerline reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial regional connection informed by historical hydrographic mean-flow context and source naming conventions. Not a simultaneous observation, monthly climatological axis or annual geometry.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"eastern regional reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#south-indian-eastern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1029/96JC03455\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 1,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 1\r\n    },\r\n    \"ANTA\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Antarctic\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"APLR\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Austral polar\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [],\r\n      \"current_count\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"BPLR\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"Boreal polar\",\r\n      \"route_candidates\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"north-cape-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-cape\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Cape Current — Northern branch\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"Declared western Hopen Deep Northern-branch study-area reach, from an OSW southern Hopen approach gate near 30 E, 75 N to the LS05 frontal/core neighborhood near 28.5 E, 77 N. Excludes Barents Sea entrance, Central branch, eastern continuations and cyclonic recirculation loops. Not the full North Cape Current or an observed trajectory.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Northern-branch Atlantic-water jet context. Fig. 9 LS05 vectors average 20–80 m; no uniform fixed-depth axis is established along this editorial reach. The separate 15-crossing fitted-width composite retains unresolved depth support.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Editorial geographic reach informed by Morozov et al. (2017) study in 2007, with general branch geography from IMR/PINRO (2009). Not a dated observed axis, annual mean or seasonal route.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"western Hopen Northern-branch reach\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#north-cape-northern-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://physical-oceanography.ru/repository/issues/2017/02/05/20170205.pdf\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"norwegian-coastal\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Norwegian Coastal Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW southern Norwegian Skagerrak approach to the Ingoy section at the Barents Sea entrance, following a simplified offshore coastal corridor. Excludes Baltic source-water transit, Jutland inflow, fjord circuits, offshore Norwegian Atlantic Current branches, West Spitsbergen and downstream Murman continuation. No whole connected-system length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Buoyant coastal-water naming context; no depth-specific core, full transverse section or uniform salinity footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography described by Christensen et al. (2026), with Ingoy context from Skagseth et al. (2011). Not a dated observed track, annual mean axis or seasonal geometry series.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"Norwegian coastal corridor to Ingoy\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/19/2785/2026/\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 54,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"candidate_id\": \"west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"current_id\": \"west-spitsbergen\",\r\n          \"name\": \"West Spitsbergen Current\",\r\n          \"scope\": \"OSW reference corridor from a selected Barents Sea opening northward-departure approach at 73 N, west of Bear Island and Svalbard, to a selected pre-branching gate near 79.6 N. Excludes upstream Norwegian Atlantic routes, eastward Barents inflow, offshore Front Current feeder, westward recirculation, shelf/fjord intrusions and downstream Svalbard/Yermak/Yermak Pass branches. No whole connected Arctic pathway length.\",\r\n          \"layer\": \"Atlantic-water boundary-flow naming context, with upper-slope and lower-slope components distinguished in source. Menze et al. mapped 20-500 m depth-averaged summer flow near the northern branch region; no depth-specific axis or uniform full-width footprint reconstructed.\",\r\n          \"time_convention\": \"Regional geography from 2018/2019 papers. Northern pathway observations span summers 2014-2017; this selected approach route is not a dated summer track, annual mean axis or seasonal geometry.\",\r\n          \"comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n          \"route_extent_kind\": \"West Spitsbergen approach corridor\",\r\n          \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n          \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/2017JC013553\",\r\n          \"nominal_crossing\": true,\r\n          \"crossing_scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n          \"crosses_in_all_declared_scenarios\": true\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"current_count\": 3,\r\n      \"nominal_current_count\": 3\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"0a46e99e2baade6512cb7781f6bdef389dbb28d238440791ba13aa79e23238b8"},"research/oyashio-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Factual regional geography paraphrased with attribution; no source figures, model fields or particle tracks packaged.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.15,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.15\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.15,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.15\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1.8,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 3,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.6,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Scientific review of naming limits, layer and regional gate conventions.\",\r\n    \"Verify bathymetric and velocity correspondence; coarse land clearance does not establish a current axis.\",\r\n    \"Canonical admission and publication review; retain regional scope and editorial provenance.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"oyashio\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Oyashio\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Selected southwestward Oyashio corridor south of Bussol Strait, followed by the first intrusion along eastern Honshu, to an OSW nominal gate at 40 N. Alternative southern gates use seasonal index limits at 38.5 N in April and 41.5 N in December. Excludes upstream East Kamchatka Current, Sea of Okhotsk circuits, offshore return branch into Subarctic Current, eastward Oyashio Extension/front and detached eddies. This branch convention is not the complete Oyashio system.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean regional corridor with a southern gate informed by the 5 C isotherm at 100 m. A temperature-defined intrusion index is not a velocity axis; no fixed-depth core or isotherm geometry extracted.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Regional naming with alternative seasonal intrusion-index gates; 40 N is an OSW intermediate comparison choice, not an annual-mean endpoint. No contemporary dated axis or seasonal length observations.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/Qiu_EoOS2019.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"The Oyashio Current, printed pp. 391-392 / PDF indices 7-8: naming south of Bussol Strait, split after Hokkaido, first intrusion and seasonal 100 m temperature-defined limits. Figure 11 caption on p. 393 specifies the JMA index region.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Qiu (2019), Kuroshio and Oyashio Currents, Encyclopedia of Ocean Sciences, 3rd edition, 384-394, doi:10.1016/B978-0-12-409548-9.11295-3.\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW chooses the Pacific-side start at 151.8 E / 46.2 N south of Bussol Strait, all longitudes and coarse vertices. The source locates the strait at 151.5 E / 46.5 N; this route does not traverse it. April/December alternatives change only the southern gate. All waypoints remain editorial and no source map or temperature contour is digitized.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      151.8,\r\n      46.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      150,\r\n      45\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      147.5,\r\n      43.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      146,\r\n      42.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      144,\r\n      41\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      143,\r\n      40\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three southern gate conventions crossed with longitude and independent endpoint latitude offsets: 81 editorial scenarios, not statistical uncertainty or an observed seasonal length distribution.\",\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1340,\r\n    225,\r\n    130,\r\n    115\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"South of Bussol Strait\",\r\n    \"40 N intrusion gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Qiu (2019), pp. 391-393\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Oyashio first-intrusion route\",\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"april_intrusion_index_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          151.8,\r\n          46.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          150,\r\n          45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          147.5,\r\n          43.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          146,\r\n          42.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          144,\r\n          41\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          143,\r\n          40\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          142.8,\r\n          39\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          142.5,\r\n          38.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"April 38.5 N temperature-index gate, with editorial connecting vertices; not an observed April axis.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"december_intrusion_index_gate\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          151.8,\r\n          46.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          150,\r\n          45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          147.5,\r\n          43.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          146,\r\n          42.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          145,\r\n          41.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"December 41.5 N temperature-index gate; no seasonal velocity field reconstructed.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [],\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"43517f3d417010f46a473f622a81bf5fa41c58e386caa3df80d089b8713fa5e3\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 996.32,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 1000,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    735.254,\r\n    1197.112\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    700,\r\n    1200\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.15,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.15,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.15,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          151.65,\r\n          46.050000000000004\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          149.85,\r\n          45\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          147.35,\r\n          43.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          145.85,\r\n          42.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          143.85,\r\n          41\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          142.85,\r\n          39.85\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"length_km\": 999.008,\r\n      \"atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"KURO\",\r\n        \"PSAW\"\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.15,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -0.15,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offse