n east of 110 W are excluded. The section gates truncate a larger current; interpolating bends are editor-selected, not a measured continuous centerline or particle path.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Subsurface northern Tsuchiya Jet, distinct from upper-ocean NECC and equatorial EUC. Source Table 1 gives local mean peak depths of 220 m at 155 W and 130 m at 110 W; these are local supports, not a uniform depth or full vertical boundaries.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of mean hydrographic-section peak locations in Johnson and Moore (1997). Historical source compilation 1967-1996 has uneven sampling; no exact regional observation period, monthly axis or dated route reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: north SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 N/220 m and 110 W 4.5 N/130 m. Transport integration latitude limits and 700-dbar reference are separately defined; they are not route width or a uniform axis layer.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Johnson and Moore (1997), The Pacific Subsurface Countercurrents and an Inertial Model, Journal of Physical Oceanography 27, 2448-2459.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"NOAA-hosted article states not subject to U.S. copyright; published by AMS in 1997. Regional facts paraphrased; source figures and historical CTD fields not packaged.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW adopts rounded Table 1 core neighborhoods at 155 W 3.5 N and 110 W 4.5 N as truncation gates. Intermediate 140 W 3.8 N and 125 W 4.2 N are editor-selected connections, not digitized axis points. The path neither assigns a whole-current origin/termination nor merges northern/southern jets or NEUC.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -155,\r\n      3.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -140,\r\n      3.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -125,\r\n      4.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -110,\r\n      4.5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_editorial_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -155,\r\n          3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -140,\r\n          4.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -125,\r\n          4.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -110,\r\n          4.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW northward bend assumption; not a width boundary or seasonal axis.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_editorial_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -155,\r\n          3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -140,\r\n          3.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -125,\r\n          3.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -110,\r\n          4.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW southward bend assumption; not a width boundary or seasonal axis.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared shapes crossed with uniform longitude offsets -0.25/0/+0.25 and independent endpoint-latitude offsets -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees: 81 editorial cases, not width bounds, seasonal extrema or confidence intervals.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review interpolation against compatible northern Tsuchiya Jet velocity fields; selected section gates are not origins or terminations.\",\r\n    \"Resolve western formation and eastward turning/merging separately from this studied reach.\",\r\n    \"Extract month/depth-resolved axes before annual length or width ranges.\",\r\n    \"Keep NEUC at 130 E and the southern Tsuchiya branches as distinct identities; no transported-volume-to-length or integration-band-to-width conversion.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    125,\r\n    320,\r\n    255,\r\n    150\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 3.3,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 5.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 1,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"155 W mean core\",\r\n    \"110 W mean core\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Johnson & Moore (1997)\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W northern Tsuchiya reach\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john2337/zonal_velocity.shtml\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Johnson et al. (2002), Direct measurements of upper ocean currents and water properties across the tropical Pacific during the 1990s.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 3.1: northern subsurface countercurrent/Tsuchiya name; 140 W around 4 N/200 m; eastward shoaling and mean/synoptic differences.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Later naming and layer context; not an additional dated or uniform-depth route.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"context_landmarks\": [],\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"da6d4d0b9b5422e4762a77b9f60ac766c80f662a776fbcfe224e27417af1e290\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 4998.364,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 5000,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    4996.147,\r\n    5003.917\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    4900,\r\n    5100\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.25,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degr