not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"tile_id\": \"level0_B_1\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a005500/a005505/perpetual_ocean2_EQUIREC_071_final_beauty_level0_B_1.mp4\",\r\n      \"source_id\": \"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_A_3\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"0afb68c180bb6a8528173974c6a88641f1f0a22ddc1db5683ee1f95c68760c33"},"research/pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared historical southern mean-core studied reach from 155 W 3.5 S to 110 W 5.5 S. These gates truncate the larger southern subsurface flow. Western formation, secondary-jet geometry and eastern continuation are excluded. This is one study-defined connection, not an aggregate centerline or sum of primary and secondary branches.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Southern subsurface/Tsuchiya flow. Johnson and Moore (1997) Table 1 gives local mean peak depths 250 m at 155 W and 160 m at 110 W; no uniform depth or full vertical bounds imposed. Later observations resolve primary and deeper secondary jets; their correspondence to this historical mean-core route remains a review gate.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Editorial connection of Johnson and Moore (1997) mean section support from a historical 1967-1996 CTD compilation. No exact regional observation dates, annual mean measured axis or monthly geometry reconstructed. Rowe et al. (2000) branch observations are separate context, not a second route or annual evolution series.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: south SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 S/250 m and 110 W 5.5 S/160 m. Latitude integration bands are not widths. Rowe et al. (2000), introduction and section 3e/Fig. 10 caption, distinguish primary and secondary southern jets.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Johnson and Moore (1997), The Pacific Subsurface Countercurrents and an Inertial Model, Journal of Physical Oceanography 27, 2448-2459.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"NOAA-hosted article states not subject to U.S. copyright; published by AMS in 1997. Regional facts paraphrased; source figures and historical CTD fields not packaged.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW uses rounded Table 1 mean-core neighborhoods at 155 W 3.5 S and 110 W 5.5 S as truncation gates. Intermediate 140 W 4.2 S and 125 W 4.8 S are editor-selected. No source figure, current axis or dated particle path digitized. Correspondence with later primary/secondary branch labels is not assumed.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -155,\r\n      -3.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -140,\r\n      -4.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -125,\r\n      -4.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -110,\r\n      -5.5\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"equatorward_editorial_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -155,\r\n          -3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -140,\r\n          -3.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -125,\r\n          -4.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -110,\r\n          -5.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW equatorward bend assumption, not a seasonal path or width edge.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"poleward_editorial_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -155,\r\n          -3.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -140,\r\n          -4.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -125,\r\n          -5.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -110,\r\n          -5.5\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW poleward bend assumption, not a secondary-jet path or width edge.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared shapes crossed with uniform longitude offsets -0.25/0/+0.25 and independent endpoint-latitude offsets -0.25/0/+0.25 degrees: 81 editorial cases, not width bounds, seasonal extrema or confidence intervals.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Review correspondence of historical mean-core sections to later primary/secondary labels; no branch aggregation inferred.\",\r\n    \"Review interpolation with compatible southern-jet velocity fields and independently resolve secondary-jet geometry.\",\r\n    \"Obtain month/depth axes before seasonal dimensions; source compilation years are not route observation dates.\",\r\n    \"Resolve western formation and eastern continuation; transport bands and PV-front spans must remain separate from current width.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    125,\r\n    360,\r\n    255,\r\n    150\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 3.3,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 5.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 1,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"155 W historical mean core\",\r\n    \"110 W historical mean core\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Johnson & Moore (1997)\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"155 W to 110 W historical southern mean-core reach\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://floats.pmel.noaa.gov/sites/default/files/atoms/files/gcj_1y.pdf\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Rowe, Firing and Johnson (2000), Pacific Equatorial Subsurface Countercurrent Velocity, Transport, and Potential Vorticity, JPO 30, 1172-1187.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Introduction pp. 1172-1174; data methods pp. 1174-1176; section 3e/Fig. 10 caption p. 1183.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Primary/secondary naming and unresolved splitting/independent origin; front scale is not whole-current width. No route digitized from figures.\",\r\n      \"license_note\": \"PDF states AMS copyright; no open license inferred; figures and data not packaged.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"context_landmarks\": [],\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"b56c4a0babd845461cf9ee3360043904214bd011d1381f4f813e16fd22037893\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocit