rio, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"bb9b13844a2eb7b52c2a25689a900c3f161841acf13a90240b4a7767df57eed1"},"research/persian-gulf-cascading-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"persian-gulf-saline-overflow\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Persian Gulf saline overflow\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Northern outflow/cascading reference reach: OSW upstream truncation near 26 N, then the source-described vicinity of 25deg20N,57E and 24deg50N,56deg50E. No Arabian Sea downstream route or whole-system origin/termination.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Descending Persian Gulf Water core; near 220 m neutral-buoyancy description is downstream context, not a fixed 220 m trajectory or surface-current route.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"October-November1999 GOGP99 study geography. Editorial line joins regional descriptions; not one synoptic snapshot, monthly geometry or an R13 width occupation.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00000/390/83.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Part2 author version abstract PDF1 and regional pathways discussion printed pp4-6/PDF5-7. Source supplies approximate cascade/rejoining geography, not a digitized axis.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Pous, S.P., Carton, X. and Lazure, P. (2004), Hydrology and circulation in the Strait of Hormuz and the Gulf of Oman: Results from the GOGP99 Experiment, parts 1 and 2, JGR Oceans 109, doi:10.1029/2003JC002145 and doi:10.1029/2003JC002146. Institutional author versions.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Copyright 2004 AGU; no open redistribution license assigned. Original author versions ignored; attributed geography and independent OSW sketch only.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-09\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW selects offshore regional gates and rounded vertices within the described geography. Alternative shapes shift intermediate latitudes by +/- 0.2 degree; longitude and independent endpoint-latitude shifts test drawing convention. These choices are not measured current boundaries, physical uncertainty or seasonal extrema.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      56.65,\r\n      26\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      56.9,\r\n      25.65\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      57,\r\n      25.333333333333332\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      56.833333333333336,\r\n      24.833333333333332\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"eastward_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          56.65,\r\n          26\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          57,\r\n          25.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          57,\r\n          25.333333333333332\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          56.833333333333336,\r\n          24.833333333333332\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial offshore bend; not a second occupation or measured current axis.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"straighter_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          56.65,\r\n          26\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          56.85,\r\n          25.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          57,\r\n          25.333333333333332\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          56.833333333333336,\r\n          24.833333333333332\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative interpolation among source-described regions; not physical uncertainty.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.03,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.03\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": 