retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/portugal-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/portugal-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"5b4df0813061bf7abed9182f58c2a844dd4aaa9600fe0c52264da725ba57dcef"},"research/redsox-northern-plume-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"red-sea-saline-overflow\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Red Sea saline overflow - northern plume reference reach\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared northern descending-plume regional connection from an OSW Bab-el-Mandeb approach gate toward the Figure 1 lower-channel neighborhood. Every vertex is an independent rounded editorial choice. Excludes the other branch, gully products, late equilibrated-water spreading and a whole-parent length.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Descending dense Red Sea outflow plume branch, with bottom and interfacial layers and changing equilibrium depth. Not a surface flow, fixed 100-250 m depth slab, channel width or equilibrated-water boundary undercurrent.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"REDSOX winter/summer 2001 geographic branch context; selected path is editorial, not a synoptic velocity axis or reconstructed seasonal routes. Cruises and station composites are separate occupations.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Peters et al. (2005), section 2, section 3a and Figure 1 printed571 / PDF3 identify two preferred descending plume pathways. Section5a printed575 / PDF7 describes non-synoptic velocity-supported northern reach 130 km; channel lengths / 5 km width are different objects. Source figure inspected for orientation only.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Peters, Johns, Bower and Fratantoni (2005), Mixing and Entrainment in the Red Sea Outflow Plume. Part I: Plume Structure, Journal of Physical Oceanography 35, 569-583.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Copyright 2005 American Meteorological Society. Original retained locally and ignored; independently selected OSW vertices and attributed facts only. No source figure or bathymetric curve copied.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-13\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Source supports the declared regional geography or study-domain convention. OSW selects all gates, rounded connecting vertices and alternative bends; no velocity axis or source trajectory reconstructed. Independent longitude and endpoint-latitude shifts describe drawing choices, not current width, source position errors or seasonal extrema.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      43.3,\r\n      12.7\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.45,\r\n      12.52\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.65,\r\n      12.44\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      43.9,\r\n      12.38\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      44.15,\r\n      12.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      44.27,\r\n      12.2\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          43.3,\r\n          12.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.45,\r\n          12.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.65,\r\n          12.42\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.9,\r\n          12.360000000000001\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          44.15,\r\n          12.280000000000001\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          44.27,\r\n          12.2\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative editorial bend between the declared regional gates; not a measured seasonal state.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern_bend\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          43.3,\r\n          12.7\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.45,\r\n          12.54\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.65,\r\n          12.459999999999999\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          43.9,\r\n          12.4\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          44.15,\r\n          12.32\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          44.27,\r\n          12.2\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative editorial bend between the declared regional gates; not a measured seasonal state.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.01,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.01\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.02,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.02\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared shapes with three longitude shifts and independent three-value endpoint latitude shifts: 81 retained editorial scenarios, not statistical uncertainty or annual variation.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 10,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Independently validate component/naming,layer,gates,fine coastline and bathymetry before physical admission.\",\r\n    \"Acquire compatible dated velocity geometry before measuring a current axis or seasonal dimensions.\",\r\n    \"Do not sum component reaches or transfer neighboring current/channel widths.\",\r\n    \"Whole-current dimensions,annual ranges,occupied width polygons,physical state containment and NASA identity remain unresolved.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    957,\r\n    370,\r\n    65,\r\n    80\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 0.85,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 1.36,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.25,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"43.3 E OSW gate\",\r\n    \"44.27 E OSW gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Peters et al. (2005), Figure 1\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"north