isplay overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"tile_id\": \"level0_B_1\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a000000/a005500/a005505/perpetual_ocean2_EQUIREC_071_final_beauty_level0_B_1.mp4\",\r\n      \"source_id\": \"source:d4e82da0872ed45c\",\r\n      \"zoom\": 0,\r\n      \"nominal_display_route_fraction\": 1.0,\r\n      \"scenario_display_route_fraction_range\": [\r\n        1.0,\r\n        1.0\r\n      ],\r\n      \"complete_display_route_in_all_scenarios\": true,\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Editorial reference-route/crop display overlap only; not physical current identification or dated event matching. Fraction measures equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_D_4\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/somali-winter-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/somali-winter-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"37cf752d61cfcfff451e3066e842e00f524b78400573b28ff731cf3ff12f4cda"},"research/south-atlantic-reach-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"south-atlantic\",\r\n  \"name\": \"South Atlantic Current\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Declared western intermediate-depth SAC reference reach from a 40 W, 39 S current-center context gate to the 16 W, 43 S Mid-Atlantic Ridge float-reach context gate. Excludes upstream Brazil/Falkland confluence paths, unresolved eastern-basin continuation and recirculation. Not a complete current or a digitized float trajectory.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Intermediate/Antarctic Intermediate Water context from subsurface floats; no velocity core, exact isopycnal or uniform-depth axis reconstructed. Surface STF geography does not replace this layer scope.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Study observations span December 1992–October 1996; selected route is an editorial geographic reach, not a time-mean axis, dated trajectory or seasonal curve.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://www.aoml.noaa.gov/phod/docs/boebel_et_al1999a.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.5, journal pp. 381–383 / PDF pp. 27–29: current center near 40 W, 39 S; easternmost RAFOS reach near 43 S, 16 W; large meanders and possible SAC/ACC exchange. Figure 11 is context only, not digitized.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Boebel, Schmid and Zenk (1999), Kinematic elements of Antarctic Intermediate Water in the western South Atlantic, Deep-Sea Research II 46, 355–392, doi:10.1016/S0967-0645(98)00104-0.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Elsevier article all rights reserved; cited factual anchor locations only. No source figure, curve, velocity field or float data copied.\",\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Source provides two approximate geographic anchors with different support: current-center description and farthest float reach. OSW connects them with coarse offshore waypoints and declares alternative shapes. These points do not define the whole SAC endpoints, one parcel path, uniform-depth core or measured meander length.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      -40,\r\n      -39\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -35,\r\n      -40\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -30,\r\n      -41\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -25,\r\n      -42\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -20,\r\n      -42.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      -16,\r\n      -43\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"less_southern_reach\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -40,\r\n          -39\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -35,\r\n          -39\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -30,\r\n          -39.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -25,\r\n          -40\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -20,\r\n          -41\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -16,\r\n          -43\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative editorial bend between the same source anchors; not observed seasonal contraction.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"more_southern_reach\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          -40,\r\n          -39\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -35,\r\n          -42\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -30,\r\n          -44\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -25,\r\n          -44\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -20,\r\n          -43.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          -16,\r\n          -43\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Alternative editorial bend between the same source anchors; not a reconstruction of documented large meanders.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.5,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.5\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -1,\r\n    0,\r\n    1\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Three declared reach shapes crossed with uniform longitude shifts -0.5/0/+0.5 degrees and independent endpoint latitude shifts -1/0/+1 degrees: 81 editorial sensitivity scenarios, not statistical uncertainty or seasonal bounds.\",\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Validate source anchor interpretation, depth and regional naming independently; the farthest observed float reach is not a whole-current endpoint.\",\r\n    \"Acquire dated float or suitable velocity geometry before measuring physical meander length; do not transfer this reach to the surface current.\",\r\n    \"Resolve eastern-basin continuation, SAC/ACC exchange and recirculation before a full-current length.\",\r\n    \"Keep all annual dimensions and physical width unresolved; complete canonical measurement and publication review separately.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    540,\r\n    505,\r\n    390,\r\n    235\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 6,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 9,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 1,\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"40 W, 39 S context gate\",\r\n    \"16 W, 43 S float-reach gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Boebel et al. (1999), sec. 3.5\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"western intermediate SAC reach\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"50bd30f033a064af98557cb790d3c6217c369a2a8c368d744e32da7c252f8671\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between successive OSW editorial vertices; no velocity field or current core is reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"nominal_reference_path_km\": 2062.51,\r\n  \"reported_approximate_reference_path_km\": 2100,\r\n  \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2045.326,\r\n    2254.868\r\n  ],\r\n  \"reported_scenario_range_km\": [\r\n    2000,\r\n    2300\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_count\": 81,\r\n  \"scenarios\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"route_variant_id\": \"nominal\",\r\n      \"longitude_offset_degrees\": -0.5,\r\n      \"start_latitude_offset_degrees\": -1,\r\n      \"end_latitude_offset_degrees\": -1,\r\n      \"start_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"end_longitude_offset_degrees\": 0,\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [