ain suitable dated upper-ocean velocity geometry before seasonal route or representative length claims.\",\r\n    \"Canonical admission and publication review; this is an editorial regional branch length.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"tsushima\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Tsushima Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Japanese coastal-branch reference corridor from an OSW eastern Tsushima Strait approach to a western Tsugaru Strait approach. Excludes the offshore/Korean branch, Soya continuation and the separately named Tsugaru outflow. Connecting vertices do not assert uninterrupted flow or a full-system length. Downstream merges are shared circulation context, not exclusive nearshore water-parcel continuity.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean Japanese coastal branch naming context; source distinguishes coastal and offshore pathways. No depth-specific velocity axis or thermal-front width reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"General regional circulation context in Yoon et al. (2016), Yokomatsu and Kida (online 2024; issue 2025) and JMA explanatory pages. Not a contemporaneous trajectory, annual mean axis or seasonal length series.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2016JC011891\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Section 1, paragraphs beginning The TWC approaching and Part of the merged: Nearshore Branch from eastern channel to Tsugaru along Japanese coast; downstream merged branches do not preserve exclusive component identity.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Yoon et al. (2016), An east-west contrast of upper ocean heat content variation south of the subpolar front in the East/Japan Sea, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans 121, 6418-6443, doi:10.1002/2016JC011891.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.data.jma.go.jp/kaiyou/data/db/maizuru/knowledge/tsushima_current.html\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Japan Meteorological Agency, What is the Tsushima Warm Current? (Japanese explanatory page), accessed 2026-10-03.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Opening paragraph and section Tsushima Warm Current pathway.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Tsushima inflow, Tsugaru/Soya exits and often discontinuous flow context; not coordinates, a measured axis or branch length.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10872-023-00693-6\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Ohshima and Kuga (2023), 50-year volume transport of the Soya Warm Current estimated from the sea-level difference and its relationship with the Tsushima and Tsugaru Warm Currents, doi:10.1007/s10872-023-00693-6.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 1, first paragraph.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Japan Sea Throughflow inflow/outflow naming; no merger of Tsushima, Tsugaru and Soya lengths.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10872-024-00734-8\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Yokomatsu and Kida (2025; online 2024), doi:10.1007/s10872-024-00734-8.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 2.1.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Coastal versus offshore broad pathway classification; not a contradictory claim that every source uses exactly two branches.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"Every vertex and gate is OSW-selected offshore reference geography. Sources support named branch and inlet/outlet context but do not publish this axis, exact named endpoints or whole-current length. Alternative approach gates test regional convention. Shelf/bathymetry and island clearance require separate review. Neither 100 m thermal-front contours, 10 C warm-water area index nor Tsushima Strait dimensions are current width; no seasonal geometry digitized.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      130,\r\n      34.15\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      131,\r\n      34.65\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      132.5,\r\n      35.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      134,\r\n      35.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      135.5,\r\n      36.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      136.25,\r\n      37.1\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      136.8,\r\n      37.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      138,\r\n      38.55\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      139,\r\n      39.3\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      139.45,\r\n      40.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      139.65,\r\n      41.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      139.9,\r\n      41.45\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"shorter_inlet_outlet_approaches\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          130.15,\r\n          34.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          131,\r\n          34.65\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          132.5,\r\n          35.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          134,\r\n          35.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          135.5,\r\n          36.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          136.25,\r\n          37.1\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          136.8,\r\n          37.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          138,\r\n          38.55\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          139,\r\n          39.3\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          139.45,\r\n          40.2\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          139.6,\r\n          41.1\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"OSW shorter inlet and western Tsugaru approaches on the same Japanese coastal corridor; not an alternative offshore/Korean branch or observed seasonal path.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Two regional approach-gate conventions crossed with longitude and independent endpoint latitude offsets -0.05/0/+0.05 degrees: 54 editorial scenarios, not branch persistence, seasonal variation or measured endpoint/width uncertainty.\",\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1320,\r\n    255,\r\n    82,\r\n    78\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"Eastern strait approach\",\r\n    \"Western Tsugaru gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Yoon et al. (2016); JMA\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"Japanese coastal branch corridor\",\r\n  \"i