s equirectangular display line, not physical kilometres.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"nasa_tiles_sha256\": \"52c6605c32e59f50aa4abde984489c7055c0e3e201e7323e30160a623c9666e0\",\r\n  \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_C_1\",\r\n  \"nasa_crop_recommendation_rule\": \"Highest zoom crop covering the entire display route in every retained scenario, with tile ID as deterministic tie-break. No physical identification asserted.\",\r\n  \"input_file\": \"research/west-spitsbergen-reference-path-input.json\",\r\n  \"figure\": \"figures/west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate.svg\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"cd6c83f417d6aa8c73303be20ad3d2472f67769c43141e08e6619ca5b996fdfa"},"research/western-adriatic-reference-path-candidate.json":{"source_json":"{\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n  \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n  \"crs\": \"OGC:CRS84\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Source regional geography paraphrased with attribution; no source figures, curves or velocity data packaged.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.05,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.05\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"map_label_size\": 1,\r\n  \"legend_line_spacing\": 1.8,\r\n  \"map_symbol_scale\": 0.4,\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Scientific review of named-flow gates and regional scope.\",\r\n    \"Verify shelf/slope correspondence with reproducible bathymetry or suitable velocity data.\",\r\n    \"Canonical admission and publication review; these are editorial route lengths.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-input.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"western-adriatic\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Western Adriatic Current\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Po-region offshore approach to western Otranto along the Italian Adriatic coast. Regional surface route, not the whole vertically structured western Adriatic circulation. Excludes eastern boundary inflow, cross-basin gyre circuits, Gulf of Manfredonia recirculation, deep dense-water pathways and downstream Ionian continuation.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Near-surface coastal corridor. No bottom/slope dense-water branch or fixed-depth velocity core reconstructed.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Regional surface naming convention informed by 1990-2007 drifter context and 2018 regional synthesis. Not a simultaneous drifter trajectory, annual mean axis or route valid during every wind reversal.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/9/713/2013/os-9-713-2013.pdf\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Poulain and Hariri (2013), section 3, printed p. 716: southeastward Italian-coast WAC exits western Otranto. Sections 2.1-2.2 and figure 1: 1990-2007 near-surface drifters and distinct outflow section; 40 N is a basin residence-time boundary, not a current endpoint.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Poulain and Hariri (2013), Transit and residence times in the Adriatic Sea surface as derived from drifter data and Lagrangian numerical simulations, Ocean Science 9, 713-720, doi:10.5194/os-9-713-2013.\",\r\n  \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/1461/2018/\",\r\n      \"citation\": \"Sciascia et al. (2018), Linking sardine recruitment in coastal areas to ocean currents using surface drifters and HF radar: a case study in the Gulf of Manfredonia, Adriatic Sea, doi:10.5194/os-14-1461-2018.\",\r\n      \"locator\": \"Section 2.1: buoyant Po-forced WAC along Italian coast and wind modulation; section 2.2: separate Gulf of Manfredonia setting.\",\r\n      \"role\": \"Surface branch identity and regional origin; local HF radar/larval paths do not define the full current axis.\"\r\n    }\r\n