onal gate coordinates are OSW choices. Excludes the South Australian segment, East Australian Current and offshore eddy excursions; not the full western/southern Australian boundary-flow system.\",\r\n  \"layer\": \"Upper-ocean shelf-edge reference geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived axis.\",\r\n  \"time_convention\": \"Source's winter boundary-flow component convention; not a simultaneous observed trajectory or guaranteed year-round path.\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2003JC001921\",\r\n  \"source_locator\": \"Ridgway and Condie (2004), section 9 paragraph 58: Zeehan flow along western Tasmania, beyond its southern tip to the southern east coast; paragraph 57 defines preceding South Australian component.\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Ridgway and Condie (2004), The 5500-km-long boundary flow off western and southern Australia, Journal of Geophysical Research: Oceans 109, C04017, doi:10.1029/2003JC001921.\",\r\n  \"source_license\": \"Factual geography only; no source prose, figure, source curve or velocity field packaged.\",\r\n  \"coordinate_selection\": \"OSW chooses coarse offshore waypoints and regional start/end gates; no source-published axis or exact nomenclature boundary is traced. Southern east-coast termination remains a regional convention.\",\r\n  \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n    [\r\n      143,\r\n      -40\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      143.8,\r\n      -41.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      144.5,\r\n      -42.5\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      145.5,\r\n      -43.8\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      147,\r\n      -44.2\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      148.2,\r\n      -43.7\r\n    ],\r\n    [\r\n      148.4,\r\n      -43\r\n    ]\r\n  ],\r\n  \"alternative_routes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"southern_tip_only\",\r\n      \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\r\n        [\r\n          143,\r\n          -40\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          143.8,\r\n          -41.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          144.5,\r\n          -42.5\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          145.5,\r\n          -43.8\r\n        ],\r\n        [\r\n          147,\r\n          -44.2\r\n        ]\r\n      ],\r\n      \"interpretation\": \"Shorter convention ending offshore of the southern tip; omits the source-described east-coast continuation.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"scenario_rule\": \"Southern-tip and southern-east-coast termination conventions crossed with three longitude offsets (-0.15/0/+0.15 degrees) and independent endpoint latitude shifts (-0.25/0/+0.25 degrees): 54 editorial scenarios, not empirical uncertainty.\",\r\n  \"longitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.15,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.15\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_latitude_offsets_degrees\": [\r\n    -0.25,\r\n    0,\r\n    0.25\r\n  ],\r\n  \"report_rounding_km\": 100,\r\n  \"rank_eligible_published_estimates\": false,\r\n  \"candidate_comparison_group\": \"osw_approximate_reference_routes\",\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Scientific review of Zeehan component gates and southern east-coast continuation.\",\r\n    \"Check shelf/slope correspondence with reproducible bathymetric or velocity data.\",\r\n    \"Canonical admission and publication review; retain changing seasonal scope and separate system measurement.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"map_view_box\": [\r\n    1300,\r\n    560,\r\n    180,\r\n    180\r\n  ],\r\n  \"endpoint_labels\": [\r\n    \"Western Bass approach\",\r\n    \"Southern east-coast gate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"figure_source_label\": \"Ridgway & Condie (2004)\",\r\n  \"route_extent_kind\": \"winter Zeehan component\",\r\n  \"whole_system_length\": false,\r\n  \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-02\",\r\n  \"input_sha256\": \"ceb337756ebc6ec247712f761c08aad4ff9ea84e9e179fc30c544a0650af9162\",\r\n  \"generator_file\": \"analysis/build_current_reference_path_candidate.py\",\r\n  \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n  \"method\": \"Sum shortest WGS84 geodesic distances between succe